WEBVTT

1
00:02:02,613 --> 00:02:06,655
Demons spent eons trying to conquer death.

2
00:02:07,113 --> 00:02:10,988
But their greed to rule the universe
led to their downfall.

3
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:12,572
Even in the Kali Yuga,

4
00:02:12,738 --> 00:02:15,530
mankind still seeks immortality.

5
00:02:15,905 --> 00:02:17,905
Yet they cannot comprehend

6
00:02:18,405 --> 00:02:22,113
that God is both
the beginning and the end.

7
00:02:22,488 --> 00:02:26,280
Still, they search for a way
to conquer death.

8
00:02:26,988 --> 00:02:30,280
What power governs the universe today?

9
00:02:30,947 --> 00:02:31,988
And where does it dwell?

10
00:02:37,322 --> 00:02:40,697
Zulfi! Was this the place
where Abdali fought in 1757?

11
00:02:43,405 --> 00:02:46,488
Prabhakar's research papers
mention this very place.

12
00:02:50,863 --> 00:02:52,822
Tesla!

13
00:03:01,238 --> 00:03:02,863
Tesla! Give me your hand.

14
00:03:03,613 --> 00:03:04,238
Come on!

15
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:57,625
Abdali!

16
00:04:05,988 --> 00:04:07,572
Come!

17
00:04:15,488 --> 00:04:17,738
Abdali!

18
00:04:39,905 --> 00:04:41,697
Come!

19
00:04:53,655 --> 00:04:55,738
Come!

20
00:04:56,197 --> 00:05:01,252
Have you come, Abdali?

21
00:05:08,863 --> 00:05:12,072
Have you come, Abdali?

22
00:05:42,697 --> 00:05:46,072
Remember this, Afghan Sultan Abdali.

23
00:05:46,613 --> 00:05:49,905
We both have the same goal.

24
00:05:50,697 --> 00:05:53,613
To open the Nagabandha gate.

25
00:05:53,697 --> 00:05:56,405
To rule over this creation.

26
00:06:00,113 --> 00:06:06,405
For that to happen,
The keys to opening that gate,

27
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:11,405
the Sacred Lotus,
and the Garuda mantras,

28
00:06:11,488 --> 00:06:13,530
must fall into our hands.

29
00:06:13,572 --> 00:06:16,072
Find them, wherever they may be.

30
00:06:19,613 --> 00:06:20,613
Go!

31
00:06:23,322 --> 00:06:24,780
Go!

32
00:09:04,863 --> 00:09:05,947
Dear students!

33
00:09:06,530 --> 00:09:07,655
Assemble here.

34
00:09:10,113 --> 00:09:11,238
Remember one thing.

35
00:09:11,572 --> 00:09:15,863
You would need a lifetime to find
even one of the artefacts shown here.

36
00:09:16,322 --> 00:09:19,363
Yet one man discovered them all.

37
00:09:19,905 --> 00:09:22,738
The longest-serving director
in Indian archaeology,

38
00:09:23,613 --> 00:09:30,113
a man capable of deciphering
any archaeological inscription,

39
00:09:30,322 --> 00:09:33,155
I present to you
the archaeological genius, Mr. Prabhakar.

40
00:09:42,780 --> 00:09:44,905
Welcome, sir. Please.

41
00:09:47,988 --> 00:09:50,822
-[all] Pleasure to meet you, sir!
-Thank you. Thank you!

42
00:09:51,322 --> 00:09:55,572
Sir, the world knows
about your achievements and legacy.

43
00:09:55,988 --> 00:09:57,405
But your failure…

44
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:03,988
Sir? Sir!

45
00:10:10,488 --> 00:10:12,905
Some questions shape the future.

46
00:10:13,655 --> 00:10:14,863
And some others…

47
00:10:16,280 --> 00:10:17,572
haunt the past.

48
00:10:17,988 --> 00:10:19,488
What exactly is it, sir?

49
00:10:23,322 --> 00:10:26,822
The Virata Purusha form
Vishnu assumed on Earth,

50
00:10:28,488 --> 00:10:32,072
a marvel before which
even the mighty Himalayas bowed.

51
00:10:34,988 --> 00:10:38,405
He who turned the infinite cosmos
into a lotus and bore it upon his navel…

52
00:10:40,113 --> 00:10:42,238
a temple dedicated to that Virata Purusha.

53
00:10:42,988 --> 00:10:44,488
The search for it

54
00:10:45,280 --> 00:10:50,072
consumed thirty years
of my life and experience.

55
00:10:51,530 --> 00:10:53,072
This defeat isn't mine alone.

56
00:10:54,197 --> 00:10:56,697
It left a bitter mark
on many throughout history.

57
00:10:57,072 --> 00:11:00,197
-So there's no path to it now, sir?
-There is.

58
00:11:02,280 --> 00:11:05,613
In 1757, Sultan Abdali
of Afghanistan and his minister

59
00:11:05,988 --> 00:11:11,530
supposedly wrote a book about
the temple attack and the path to it.

60
00:11:12,530 --> 00:11:14,113
This inscription claims so.

61
00:11:14,447 --> 00:11:17,488
That book is the only guide to the path.

62
00:11:18,030 --> 00:11:20,405
So … where is that book, sir?

63
00:11:38,155 --> 00:11:40,197
-Sir. Tesla here.
-Yes, Tesla.

64
00:11:40,322 --> 00:11:43,280
-I must speak to Mr. Prabhakar urgently.
-Wait a minute.

65
00:11:45,780 --> 00:11:48,447
Sir! Tesla is on the phone.

66
00:11:49,947 --> 00:11:50,947
He says it's urgent.

67
00:11:56,488 --> 00:11:57,697
-Sorry! Sorry!
-Hey!

68
00:11:58,572 --> 00:12:00,780
-[in Hindi] Watch where you're going!
-Please forgive me.

69
00:12:00,988 --> 00:12:02,363
-Where do these people come from?
-Sorry.

70
00:12:12,863 --> 00:12:14,738
Stop! Stop!
[in Hindi] Do you have a pass?

71
00:12:15,488 --> 00:12:18,613
-Sir!
-Security, let him in.

72
00:12:19,030 --> 00:12:21,572
-He's our guy.
-Okay, sir! Go!

73
00:12:31,488 --> 00:12:33,738
This summit
will greatly benefit the country.

74
00:12:33,863 --> 00:12:36,565
-Your support is vital for our nation.
-Mr. Murali Prasad!

75
00:12:38,530 --> 00:12:40,863
Prabhakar? Excuse me.

76
00:12:43,738 --> 00:12:44,697
Yes, Prabhakar.

77
00:12:45,572 --> 00:12:48,238
I need to meet the Prime Minister
immediately. It's an important matter.

78
00:12:49,655 --> 00:12:51,072
Everything here is important.

79
00:12:51,572 --> 00:12:53,822
No one meets the Prime Minister casually.

80
00:12:54,738 --> 00:12:57,488
We have rules and protocols.

81
00:12:58,572 --> 00:13:00,988
Come to the office tomorrow morning.
We'll discuss it then.

82
00:13:01,113 --> 00:13:03,947
Sir, it's very important.

83
00:13:05,113 --> 00:13:05,947
Who is he?

84
00:13:05,988 --> 00:13:09,197
He's Tesla, an archaeology
research scholar.

85
00:13:09,405 --> 00:13:10,905
-Oh!
-Trust me.

86
00:13:11,363 --> 00:13:13,363
This is going to change India's future.

87
00:13:13,780 --> 00:13:15,863
This meeting
is also about Indians' future.

88
00:13:16,655 --> 00:13:20,780
The inscriptions and relics
you discover won't change the future.

89
00:13:21,697 --> 00:13:24,447
But… policies will change India

90
00:13:24,863 --> 00:13:26,822
by creating big wealth.

91
00:13:27,113 --> 00:13:29,405
Sir, what you're talking about

92
00:13:29,530 --> 00:13:31,697
is the wealth
India may gain in the future.

93
00:13:32,363 --> 00:13:34,822
But what I'm talking about

94
00:13:35,655 --> 00:13:38,905
is the immense wealth
already hidden in this country.

95
00:13:40,780 --> 00:13:43,947
Come on, Tesla!
Prabhakar, enjoy the evening.

96
00:13:44,780 --> 00:13:45,822
Sir, hear me out!

97
00:13:46,780 --> 00:13:48,113
It's about Nagabandham.

98
00:13:51,780 --> 00:13:53,113
What nonsense are you talking?

99
00:13:54,697 --> 00:13:56,197
Do you even know what you're saying?

100
00:13:57,030 --> 00:14:00,405
This isn't what you told me before!
You think this is a joke?

101
00:14:02,155 --> 00:14:04,530
People have only heard about Nagabandham.
No one has ever seen it.

102
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:08,197
Our archaeology department
has researched it for years.

103
00:14:08,488 --> 00:14:09,863
We never found a single clue.

104
00:14:10,822 --> 00:14:12,072
But, I've got it, sir.

105
00:14:57,780 --> 00:14:58,655
Alright.

106
00:14:59,530 --> 00:15:01,197
You wait here, I'll come back.

107
00:15:05,738 --> 00:15:06,947
-Please!
-Of course!

108
00:15:08,155 --> 00:15:08,988
Sir!

109
00:15:12,238 --> 00:15:13,113
Sure!

110
00:15:14,113 --> 00:15:14,947
Okay!

111
00:15:16,113 --> 00:15:18,572
The PM wants to see you
at his residence tomorrow at 8 AM.

112
00:15:18,655 --> 00:15:20,155
-Okay, see you.
-Okay.

113
00:15:28,113 --> 00:15:30,488
-Sir, sir!
-Yes!

114
00:15:30,738 --> 00:15:34,322
[in Hindi] Sir! Please, sir!
Please buy a toy, sir.

115
00:15:34,572 --> 00:15:37,572
Please, sir!
Please buy a toy, sir.

116
00:15:37,738 --> 00:15:39,655
-Please, sir!
-How much?

117
00:15:40,197 --> 00:15:41,613
Give me whatever you can, sir.

118
00:15:44,155 --> 00:15:45,405
Brother, whose vehicle is this?

119
00:15:47,072 --> 00:15:49,572
This is India, sir. We'll change India.

120
00:15:54,488 --> 00:15:55,363
Robert, stop the car.

121
00:16:03,113 --> 00:16:04,655
-Bye, sir!
-Tesla!

122
00:16:05,113 --> 00:16:07,322
-Yes, sir.
-Don't overthink it.

123
00:16:07,738 --> 00:16:10,155
It's Riya's birthday today.
Let's meet for dinner.

124
00:16:10,572 --> 00:16:12,363
-Hmm.
-Okay, sir. I'll see you.

125
00:16:28,447 --> 00:16:29,322
Riya!

126
00:16:30,687 --> 00:16:31,270
Daddy!

127
00:16:32,530 --> 00:16:33,863
Come on my dear baby!

128
00:16:37,405 --> 00:16:40,405
-Happy Birthday, baby! I love you!
-Thank you, Daddy.

129
00:16:41,155 --> 00:16:41,988
Where's my gift?

130
00:16:42,863 --> 00:16:45,863
-I must've forgotten it in the car.
-It's okay, give after some time.

131
00:16:45,905 --> 00:16:47,197
-Are you sure? Come!
-I'm sure.

132
00:16:47,447 --> 00:16:48,780
-Come!
-Mom and I've been waiting

133
00:16:48,863 --> 00:16:50,572
for you for so long.

134
00:16:50,655 --> 00:16:52,238
-Tessie!
-I'm sorry, baby!

135
00:16:53,197 --> 00:16:54,197
Why are you so late?

136
00:16:54,280 --> 00:16:55,238
Ah… Father!

137
00:16:55,488 --> 00:16:57,988
-Yes, my son?
-I have to make a confession.

138
00:16:59,072 --> 00:16:59,617
Come!

139
00:17:00,155 --> 00:17:01,530
Riya, go to mom.

140
00:17:03,238 --> 00:17:03,988
Come baby!

141
00:17:07,238 --> 00:17:08,738
Praise the Lord, Father!

142
00:17:08,863 --> 00:17:12,155
I made a mistake
hiding the truth about Zulfikar.

143
00:17:12,322 --> 00:17:17,363
Show me how I can atone for my mistake…

144
00:17:25,488 --> 00:17:26,280
Tesla!

145
00:17:33,363 --> 00:17:35,863
Praise the Lord, my son.

146
00:18:09,030 --> 00:18:11,780
-You?
-Yes, I am…

147
00:18:12,947 --> 00:18:15,322
the father of all sins.

148
00:18:26,613 --> 00:18:28,238
You just confessed…

149
00:18:29,072 --> 00:18:29,947
My son!

150
00:18:31,091 --> 00:18:32,799
Shall I tell you how to atone?

151
00:18:37,572 --> 00:18:39,780
Who decides

152
00:18:40,572 --> 00:18:43,613
the winner and loser

153
00:18:45,113 --> 00:18:46,905
in this game we played?

154
00:18:48,655 --> 00:18:49,613
It's me!

155
00:18:50,530 --> 00:18:51,988
You cheat! I'll kill you!

156
00:18:55,113 --> 00:18:55,947
Daddy!

157
00:18:55,988 --> 00:18:56,822
Let me go!

158
00:18:57,072 --> 00:18:58,113
Mommy.

159
00:19:15,863 --> 00:19:17,655
Tesla!

160
00:19:20,655 --> 00:19:21,780
Mommy!

161
00:19:26,030 --> 00:19:27,322
Hey, Tesla!

162
00:19:27,572 --> 00:19:28,488
Where is the book?

163
00:19:28,655 --> 00:19:30,697
-Tesla!
-Tell me! Tell me!

164
00:19:31,863 --> 00:19:33,238
Daddy!

165
00:19:36,780 --> 00:19:42,405
Your… your scheme for the Nagabandham…

166
00:19:43,447 --> 00:19:46,155
will never succeed in this lifetime!

167
00:19:48,905 --> 00:19:49,738
No!

168
00:19:50,530 --> 00:19:51,655
No! No!

169
00:19:55,947 --> 00:19:57,655
Tesla! Tesla!

170
00:19:57,738 --> 00:19:58,905
Daddy!

171
00:20:01,447 --> 00:20:04,488
-Uncle, please… Uncle, please. No!
-Riya!

172
00:20:04,613 --> 00:20:07,280
Please leave my dad alone!

173
00:20:08,113 --> 00:20:11,155
Uncle, please release my dad!

174
00:20:11,197 --> 00:20:13,905
-Uncle! Please, uncle!
-Shh!

175
00:20:17,030 --> 00:20:19,863
Cute… cute baby.

176
00:20:20,822 --> 00:20:22,113
Were you scared?

177
00:20:23,363 --> 00:20:25,822
You don't have to be
scared, sweetheart.

178
00:20:27,155 --> 00:20:28,030
He should!

179
00:20:30,488 --> 00:20:33,405
Your dad stole my book

180
00:20:33,488 --> 00:20:34,947
and hid it somewhere.

181
00:20:35,863 --> 00:20:42,155
My mom told me
never to take what belongs to others.

182
00:20:42,530 --> 00:20:47,030
If you want, I'll give you
all the toys I have.

183
00:20:47,072 --> 00:20:49,238
No! I want that book!

184
00:20:49,572 --> 00:20:51,363
-Let's play a game.
-Uncle, No!

185
00:20:51,405 --> 00:20:52,488
Your daddy will give it to me then!

186
00:20:53,113 --> 00:20:54,988
-What do you want?
-Uncle…

187
00:20:55,447 --> 00:20:56,947
What exactly do you want?

188
00:20:57,863 --> 00:20:58,780
Ask him.

189
00:21:01,572 --> 00:21:03,363
What's that book, Tesla?

190
00:21:03,905 --> 00:21:05,238
What's that book, Tesla?

191
00:21:07,488 --> 00:21:10,738
She's asking you, isn't she? Tell her!

192
00:21:12,030 --> 00:21:15,697
No matter how many lifetimes you live,

193
00:21:16,238 --> 00:21:17,572
you will never get it!

194
00:21:18,988 --> 00:21:21,988
Don't do this uncle! Please uncle!

195
00:21:25,697 --> 00:21:26,530
No!

196
00:21:31,072 --> 00:21:32,738
Uncle, don't!

197
00:21:56,322 --> 00:21:57,697
Riya, come back!

198
00:22:00,030 --> 00:22:02,488
Riya, just stay here!

199
00:22:03,655 --> 00:22:05,988
Mommy! Uncle, no!

200
00:22:06,238 --> 00:22:08,280
-No, no! No, Uncle! No!
-Riya, come back!

201
00:22:10,030 --> 00:22:12,322
No… uncle…

202
00:22:13,113 --> 00:22:15,572
Uncle! No!

203
00:22:16,280 --> 00:22:17,280
Mommy!

204
00:22:19,822 --> 00:22:23,447
I will do as you said.
Please let my mommy go…

205
00:22:26,572 --> 00:22:27,530
Mommy!

206
00:22:30,822 --> 00:22:33,155
That's exactly what I'm saying, baby.

207
00:22:33,530 --> 00:22:36,530
But your daddy isn't listening.
What can I do?

208
00:22:36,822 --> 00:22:38,905
Give me the book and I'll let you all go.

209
00:22:39,822 --> 00:22:41,280
Otherwise, your mommy…

210
00:22:44,905 --> 00:22:47,197
Daddy! Daddy!

211
00:22:48,447 --> 00:22:49,738
Where is the book, Daddy?

212
00:22:51,697 --> 00:22:52,863
-Daddy!
-Sorry!

213
00:22:56,697 --> 00:22:57,405
Daddy?

214
00:22:59,030 --> 00:23:01,488
Daddy? No…

215
00:23:05,030 --> 00:23:06,863
Daddy, wake up!

216
00:23:10,530 --> 00:23:12,697
Daddy! Mommy!

217
00:23:12,780 --> 00:23:14,113
Tesla!

218
00:23:19,572 --> 00:23:20,572
God…

219
00:23:21,655 --> 00:23:24,072
God is watching everything.

220
00:23:27,072 --> 00:23:30,405
He will surely… punish you!

221
00:23:32,322 --> 00:23:33,405
Daddy!

222
00:23:37,530 --> 00:23:38,697
Daddy!

223
00:23:39,572 --> 00:23:41,030
Ali! No!

224
00:23:41,447 --> 00:23:43,113
No! Riya!

225
00:23:58,697 --> 00:24:00,113
-Mrs. Padmamma!
-Namaste, Priest.

226
00:24:00,155 --> 00:24:02,947
The goddess Manasa Devi
is the primordial mother of all serpents.

227
00:24:03,113 --> 00:24:06,072
To that divine mother, everything offered,
be it ritual or offering, is only milk.

228
00:24:06,572 --> 00:24:09,780
Performing the first abhishekam
to the goddess with the milk you bring

229
00:24:09,905 --> 00:24:12,072
is a tradition passed down
through generations.

230
00:24:12,488 --> 00:24:15,780
-So, where are your son and daughter?
-They're coming.

231
00:24:32,613 --> 00:24:34,280
There she is! Ms. Manasa!

232
00:24:45,530 --> 00:24:47,363
It looks like Lord Shiva himself

233
00:24:47,530 --> 00:24:50,697
is carrying his child,
Manasa Devi, in his arms.

234
00:25:20,697 --> 00:25:21,905
My precious!

235
00:25:23,572 --> 00:25:24,447
Be careful!

236
00:25:26,322 --> 00:25:27,280
What is this, brother-in-law?

237
00:25:27,447 --> 00:25:30,530
Did you carry your sister
so her feet wouldn't hurt?

238
00:26:22,363 --> 00:26:23,322
Scumbag!

239
00:26:23,947 --> 00:26:24,905
Mr. Priest!

240
00:26:25,988 --> 00:26:27,780
As the festival day is auspicious,

241
00:26:28,072 --> 00:26:33,155
we've finalized Manasa's marriage
to Raju, son of Narasimha of Nagulakota.

242
00:26:33,613 --> 00:26:35,072
Say something, sister.

243
00:26:36,238 --> 00:26:37,238
What was that?

244
00:26:38,447 --> 00:26:41,238
There's already a groom in the house.
How can you marry her off to an outsider?

245
00:26:41,530 --> 00:26:42,738
What about our honor?

246
00:26:45,322 --> 00:26:48,405
We've been hoping to make Manasa
our daughter-in-law.

247
00:26:48,613 --> 00:26:49,697
No, sister-in-law.

248
00:26:50,030 --> 00:26:53,030
Raju and Manasa
have loved each other since childhood.

249
00:26:53,072 --> 00:26:56,155
Your husband died owing debts,
and that's become a burden now.

250
00:26:56,530 --> 00:26:59,530
My husband lent you our boat
so you could repay that debt, didn't he?

251
00:27:00,405 --> 00:27:03,655
You made money from it, and now
you want to marry her off to him?

252
00:27:04,405 --> 00:27:05,405
How is that fair?

253
00:27:06,405 --> 00:27:09,488
Out of the goodness of my heart,
I even overlooked that debt

254
00:27:09,530 --> 00:27:11,780
and thought of making Manasa
my daughter-in-law.

255
00:27:11,905 --> 00:27:15,030
Is our Kinka not handsome enough?
Is he not worthy?

256
00:27:15,655 --> 00:27:17,363
Hey, why aren't you talking?

257
00:27:17,780 --> 00:27:21,072
Aunt! A marriage without love
is never a good marriage.

258
00:27:21,197 --> 00:27:24,988
-Hey!
-How dare you push my sister?

259
00:27:26,155 --> 00:27:27,197
Who is your aunt?

260
00:27:27,822 --> 00:27:30,322
We don't know where you were born,
or even where you came from.

261
00:27:30,363 --> 00:27:32,197
Who are you to interfere in our matters?

262
00:27:33,447 --> 00:27:34,863
-Mom, stop it!
-Hey!

263
00:27:35,405 --> 00:27:37,530
-What your mom said is true, isn't it?
-Gandhar Raju, stop!

264
00:27:37,613 --> 00:27:38,530
Hey!

265
00:27:38,572 --> 00:27:40,530
He is an orphan
who doesn't know his mother!

266
00:27:40,863 --> 00:27:42,988
-A son who doesn't know his father!
-Hey!

267
00:27:45,280 --> 00:27:47,822
The moment you insulted my brother,
my hand rose on its own!

268
00:27:47,905 --> 00:27:49,572
One more word…

269
00:27:51,905 --> 00:27:53,238
-Hey.
-Hey…

270
00:27:53,280 --> 00:27:54,697
and I'll slash your neck.

271
00:27:54,905 --> 00:27:56,030
-Hey!
-Hey!

272
00:27:56,072 --> 00:27:56,905
Nephew!

273
00:27:58,697 --> 00:28:00,488
-Hey, stop!
-Manasa.

274
00:28:01,697 --> 00:28:02,697
I'm talking to you.

275
00:28:04,905 --> 00:28:07,655
In the name of Goddess,
I swear to everyone,

276
00:28:08,488 --> 00:28:09,530
Rudra is my son!

277
00:28:10,572 --> 00:28:11,447
My life!

278
00:28:13,905 --> 00:28:15,572
If anyone lays a hand on him

279
00:28:16,197 --> 00:28:20,155
or says even a single word against him,
I'll sever all relationship with them.

280
00:28:22,197 --> 00:28:23,155
Hey, Manasa!

281
00:28:29,363 --> 00:28:32,488
The principle was repaid,
what about the interest?

282
00:28:48,572 --> 00:28:49,655
<i>Who's your aunt?</i>

283
00:28:49,863 --> 00:28:52,405
<i>We don't know where you were born,</i>
 <i>or even where you came from.</i>

284
00:28:55,947 --> 00:28:56,780
Brother.

285
00:28:57,822 --> 00:29:00,113
Are you drinking to relive the past
and forget the present?

286
00:29:01,697 --> 00:29:02,613
I mean…

287
00:29:02,905 --> 00:29:06,738
You've been hiding away, barely eating,
ever since the incident at the fair.

288
00:29:07,822 --> 00:29:10,613
Your sister could barely open the box,
yet she came to feed you.

289
00:29:11,405 --> 00:29:14,113
Alright, done feeling sad?
Shall I feed you?

290
00:29:15,368 --> 00:29:16,201
Feed him.

291
00:29:18,697 --> 00:29:23,280
Who feels bad for people who only act
when there's something in it for them?

292
00:29:23,530 --> 00:29:26,780
-What's this, brother? Our mom trusts you.
-After you feed him, he'll forget it all.

293
00:29:27,113 --> 00:29:28,905
And you are my life.

294
00:29:29,322 --> 00:29:31,030
Really? What about me?

295
00:29:32,322 --> 00:29:35,113
-Hey, Manasa! What about me?
-Hey!

296
00:29:36,488 --> 00:29:39,697
Rudra, you shouldn't be
thinking about them right now.

297
00:29:40,072 --> 00:29:41,280
You should be thinking about our wedding.

298
00:29:42,947 --> 00:29:46,238
Everyone from the surrounding villages
should attend. It must be a grand affair.

299
00:29:47,155 --> 00:29:49,113
Even if no one attends the wedding,

300
00:29:49,155 --> 00:29:51,530
my brother being there is enough for me.

301
00:29:51,572 --> 00:29:52,738
Not even me?

302
00:29:54,697 --> 00:29:56,030
When I think about your aunt,

303
00:29:56,488 --> 00:29:58,697
I feel like she might try
to stop this wedding.

304
00:29:58,988 --> 00:30:02,030
As long as my brother is with me,
who dares to stop this wedding?

305
00:30:02,197 --> 00:30:04,447
God! Always going on about your brother!

306
00:30:04,697 --> 00:30:06,155
After marriage, instead of
you coming to my house,

307
00:30:06,322 --> 00:30:08,905
I feel like I'll come
live in your house instead.

308
00:30:08,988 --> 00:30:12,738
That's how it is!
I will stay where my heart is.

309
00:30:12,905 --> 00:30:15,697
-Alright then. It's inevitable.
-Brother, it's getting dark.

310
00:30:15,738 --> 00:30:17,905
Let's go home, Mom will be waiting.

311
00:30:18,697 --> 00:30:20,572
You go ahead, I'll come later.

312
00:30:20,863 --> 00:30:22,280
-Come!
-Come quickly, Rudra.

313
00:30:22,863 --> 00:30:25,655
We're leaving now.
Let's meet tomorrow in Srirangapuram.

314
00:30:26,655 --> 00:30:29,405
[chanting]

315
00:30:37,322 --> 00:30:40,363
Everything will be fine
going forward, Janardhan.

316
00:30:42,280 --> 00:30:43,655
What do you mean, fine?

317
00:30:46,072 --> 00:30:49,155
The humiliation I faced at the fair today
felt like my head being cut off.

318
00:30:49,238 --> 00:30:52,322
Ignoring everything I said,
you kept supporting your sister.

319
00:30:52,613 --> 00:30:53,447
What happened now?

320
00:30:53,863 --> 00:30:56,113
Your sister's actions
haven't changed you at all.

321
00:31:07,197 --> 00:31:08,697
Sister!

322
00:31:10,197 --> 00:31:14,613
Seeing you like this
it hurts me deeply.

323
00:31:15,030 --> 00:31:18,113
Even though his sister
Padmamma insulted you so much,

324
00:31:19,238 --> 00:31:21,072
brother-in-law didn't say a word.

325
00:31:21,363 --> 00:31:23,322
He won't! Why would he?

326
00:31:23,488 --> 00:31:25,113
He loves his sister, doesn't he?

327
00:31:26,697 --> 00:31:29,572
He didn't react at all
even when they insulted me so much.

328
00:31:32,572 --> 00:31:34,697
Hey, Rudra! Come here.

329
00:31:34,988 --> 00:31:37,655
-May you live a hundred years! Come!
-Come!

330
00:31:43,488 --> 00:31:44,405
Hey!

331
00:31:45,405 --> 00:31:46,863
Rudra is one of ours!

332
00:31:47,238 --> 00:31:49,113
Go away! Move!

333
00:31:49,697 --> 00:31:50,447
I said go.

334
00:31:57,947 --> 00:31:59,238
Why did you come here?

335
00:32:00,197 --> 00:32:04,280
Uncle, I'm not old enough
to say this to you.

336
00:32:05,322 --> 00:32:06,613
What happened today was wrong.

337
00:32:07,363 --> 00:32:08,738
No matter who is responsible,

338
00:32:09,697 --> 00:32:11,197
everyone was hurt by it.

339
00:32:11,697 --> 00:32:13,738
I came here so that
this pain doesn't turn into anger.

340
00:32:14,947 --> 00:32:18,530
Whether good or bad,
you are all bound by blood.

341
00:32:19,363 --> 00:32:22,197
My sister did that out of love for me.

342
00:32:22,780 --> 00:32:25,280
She has neither
anger nor hatred toward you.

343
00:32:26,238 --> 00:32:28,280
Even if the whole village
attends her wedding,

344
00:32:28,613 --> 00:32:29,530
you're her uncle.

345
00:32:30,155 --> 00:32:32,447
Nothing can replace you.

346
00:32:33,738 --> 00:32:36,655
If I am the only problem here,
I'll leave after her wedding.

347
00:32:38,238 --> 00:32:39,447
-Hey!
-Brother!

348
00:32:39,488 --> 00:32:41,322
-Hey, Kinka! Hey.
-Who are you, man?

349
00:32:41,738 --> 00:32:43,363
What difference does it make
whether you stay or leave?

350
00:32:44,155 --> 00:32:44,780
Hey!

351
00:32:47,572 --> 00:32:49,572
-Hey!
-Brother, stop.

352
00:32:49,947 --> 00:32:52,363
That disgraceful woman is not my aunt,

353
00:32:53,238 --> 00:32:55,447
and the other worthless woman
is not my sister-in-law!

354
00:33:10,447 --> 00:33:11,613
I'll endure it.

355
00:33:12,447 --> 00:33:15,030
Call me anything you want.
I'll endure it!

356
00:33:17,155 --> 00:33:19,697
If you speak lightly
because I came to compromise,

357
00:33:20,488 --> 00:33:21,780
I will behead you.

358
00:33:22,697 --> 00:33:23,530
Is that clear?

359
00:34:19,405 --> 00:34:22,280
[Lord Rama hymn chant]

360
00:34:31,863 --> 00:34:34,988
Dear, Parvathi, your Guru is coming.

361
00:34:55,530 --> 00:34:58,072
Saraswathi,
are the prayer arrangements ready?

362
00:34:58,322 --> 00:35:00,613
Your disciple,
who knows your every routine

363
00:35:00,655 --> 00:35:04,322
-has already completed the arrangements.<i>-Namo Narayanaya.</i>

364
00:35:05,447 --> 00:35:06,947
Please bless me, Guruji.

365
00:35:07,030 --> 00:35:08,113
May you live a long life!

366
00:35:09,697 --> 00:35:11,447
She is another disciple.

367
00:35:11,863 --> 00:35:13,155
Her name is Priyamani.

368
00:35:13,238 --> 00:35:15,447
Sent by Raja Ravi Varma.

369
00:35:15,613 --> 00:35:18,488
She has come here
to learn the Vedas from you.

370
00:35:19,072 --> 00:35:22,238
Among all things in creation,
the wisdom of the Vedas alone is eternal.

371
00:35:22,863 --> 00:35:24,697
Learning the Vedas is not merely useful,

372
00:35:25,488 --> 00:35:27,655
It is a blessing.
I will definitely teach you.

373
00:35:45,988 --> 00:35:47,238
What is in that box?

374
00:35:48,072 --> 00:35:50,697
The key to the sanctum doors
of Ranganatha Swamy temple.

375
00:35:51,530 --> 00:35:52,447
And that?

376
00:35:54,155 --> 00:35:55,030
The Kunchakola.

377
00:35:55,113 --> 00:35:58,072
It is used to open the main temple doors.

378
00:35:58,988 --> 00:36:00,530
So many questions on your first day?

379
00:36:01,155 --> 00:36:02,613
I'll explain eventually.

380
00:36:28,697 --> 00:36:29,530
Greetings, sir!

381
00:37:39,030 --> 00:37:40,863
<i>Govinda Govinda!</i>

382
00:37:46,988 --> 00:37:50,072
<i>Govinda Govinda!</i>

383
00:38:27,447 --> 00:38:28,697
May you live long!

384
00:38:29,572 --> 00:38:31,197
<i>Om Namo Ranganathaya Namahā!</i>

385
00:38:33,447 --> 00:38:36,072
Are the arrangements
for the Lord's festival going well?

386
00:38:36,322 --> 00:38:40,155
By the grace of sacred chants,

387
00:38:40,613 --> 00:38:42,113
everything is going in perfect order.

388
00:38:43,155 --> 00:38:45,947
Though our family has overseen
the temple for generations,

389
00:38:46,280 --> 00:38:48,030
its true responsibility rests with you.

390
00:38:49,072 --> 00:38:53,238
As long as the temple and its traditions
are under your care, we can rest easy.

391
00:38:53,280 --> 00:38:55,613
I bow to Lord Narayana!
That is our good fortune.

392
00:38:56,488 --> 00:38:58,780
As you said, this temple is extraordinary.

393
00:38:59,738 --> 00:39:02,405
It is ancient and immensely significant.

394
00:39:04,322 --> 00:39:08,738
It is our fortune to be entrusted
with conducting these celebrations.

395
00:39:09,238 --> 00:39:11,738
May it be auspicious.
I shall take my leave.

396
00:39:12,822 --> 00:39:15,072
<i>Om Namo Narayanaya!</i>

397
00:39:15,780 --> 00:39:16,655
Wait, Parvathi.

398
00:39:16,822 --> 00:39:19,905
Guruji, may I ask a small doubt?

399
00:39:19,988 --> 00:39:20,947
Go ahead, dear.

400
00:39:21,072 --> 00:39:24,072
Every day the deity is adorned
with different decorations, right?

401
00:39:24,697 --> 00:39:28,363
Even if it's priceless, why hold
a grand festival for a golden flower?

402
00:39:29,655 --> 00:39:32,613
Festivals are not about
form or splendor, my dear.

403
00:39:32,655 --> 00:39:33,738
There she goes again.

404
00:39:33,780 --> 00:39:35,697
They are dedicated to the divine essence.

405
00:39:36,572 --> 00:39:39,780
To keep society united
and free of divisions,

406
00:39:40,405 --> 00:39:43,613
the Creator established
festivals as a sacred bond.

407
00:39:44,280 --> 00:39:47,030
It is not a golden flower,
but the Sacred Lotus.

408
00:39:47,947 --> 00:39:52,155
Its power and significance
may sound like mere folklore to you.

409
00:39:52,697 --> 00:39:55,155
-Wait. Dear Parvathi.
-Guruji?

410
00:39:55,322 --> 00:39:58,780
Can you tell this girl, in simple words,

411
00:39:59,363 --> 00:40:01,905
what you found
in your research about this temple?

412
00:40:03,197 --> 00:40:05,113
In the mid-17th century,

413
00:40:05,322 --> 00:40:07,405
this Ranganatha Swamy temple
was destroyed by fire.

414
00:40:07,655 --> 00:40:09,863
The then king, Ranga Martanda Varma

415
00:40:10,113 --> 00:40:13,363
went to the Himalayas
to rebuild the temple.

416
00:40:13,613 --> 00:40:16,155
There, while bringing Shaligram stones

417
00:40:16,197 --> 00:40:18,030
believed to be
the embodiment of Lord Vishnu

418
00:40:18,197 --> 00:40:22,613
a Naga Sadhu is said to have given him
this Sacred Lotus, as our history tells.

419
00:40:22,947 --> 00:40:27,947
That is why, every Kartika Purnima,
grand festivities are held here.

420
00:40:29,322 --> 00:40:31,988
Forgive me, Guruji.
I spoke out of ignorance.

421
00:40:33,405 --> 00:40:35,238
Young people don't ask from ignorance.

422
00:40:35,447 --> 00:40:36,905
They ask because they're curious.

423
00:40:37,947 --> 00:40:40,197
Our culture is praised by the whole world.

424
00:40:41,072 --> 00:40:43,738
Let us not diminish it. Do you understand?

425
00:40:45,363 --> 00:40:46,238
Let's go.

426
00:40:47,197 --> 00:40:49,280
Manasa, we've reached
your mother-in-law's village.

427
00:40:49,780 --> 00:40:50,613
Alright.

428
00:40:53,947 --> 00:40:54,613
Come, Rudra!

429
00:40:55,822 --> 00:40:57,613
-Brother-in-law!
-Are you sober now?

430
00:40:59,322 --> 00:41:00,363
Come!

431
00:41:02,613 --> 00:41:04,405
You look like a beautiful doll, dear.

432
00:41:05,572 --> 00:41:06,530
Your mother isn't with you?

433
00:41:06,738 --> 00:41:08,113
She's busy with the wedding preparations.

434
00:41:08,738 --> 00:41:10,363
Once you fulfill your vow to the Lord,

435
00:41:10,613 --> 00:41:12,488
you'll never have to point a weapon again.

436
00:41:12,724 --> 00:41:13,304
Come, brother.

437
00:41:13,613 --> 00:41:15,822
-You go ahead!
-Okay, you stay here. We'll be back.

438
00:41:16,738 --> 00:41:18,947
-Come on, dear.
-Hurry, the celebrations are beginning!

439
00:41:26,197 --> 00:41:31,238
<i>♪ To Srinivasa, beloved of Lakshmi</i>
 <i>Bestower of all auspiciousness ♪</i>

440
00:41:31,572 --> 00:41:36,905
<i>♪ Glory to Venkatesa</i>
 <i>Lord of Venkatagiri ♪</i>

441
00:41:37,072 --> 00:41:41,905
<i>♪ Glory to Venkatesa ♪</i>

442
00:41:42,030 --> 00:41:47,363
<i>♪ Whose divine gaze enchants Lakshmi</i>
 <i>And blesses all creation ♪</i>

443
00:41:49,322 --> 00:41:53,447
<i>♪ We bow before You</i>
 <i>Again and again ♪</i>

444
00:41:54,072 --> 00:41:58,447
<i>♪ We bow before You</i>
 <i>Again and again ♪</i>

445
00:41:58,530 --> 00:42:03,447
<i>♪ We bow before You, O Narayana</i>
 <i>Endless salutations unto You ♪</i>

446
00:42:07,780 --> 00:42:13,197
<i>♪ We bow before You, O Narayana</i>
 <i>Endless salutations unto You ♪</i>

447
00:42:13,697 --> 00:42:18,155
<i>♪ We bow before You, O Narayana</i>
 <i>You are all things, in all places ♪</i>

448
00:42:18,238 --> 00:42:23,322
<i>♪ Remembering You brings prosperity</i>
 <i>Meditating on You grants liberation ♪</i>

449
00:42:23,447 --> 00:42:28,197
<i>♪ Revered by the nine planets</i>
 <i>Salutations to You, O Narayana ♪</i>

450
00:42:28,322 --> 00:42:32,947
<i>♪ Destroyer of demons</i>
 <i>Hear our prayer ♪</i>

451
00:42:33,155 --> 00:42:37,238
<i>♪ Protect us and watch over us ♪</i>

452
00:42:37,405 --> 00:42:42,113
<i>♪ Dweller of the sacred Vamana shrine</i>
 <i>O Srinivasa, guardian of the Kali Yuga ♪</i>

453
00:42:42,197 --> 00:42:47,155
<i>♪ We take refuge in You</i>
 <i>O Lord of Vaikunta ♪</i>

454
00:42:49,488 --> 00:42:54,322
<i>♪ Salutations to Padmanabha</i>
 <i>Salutations to the soul of all existence ♪</i>

455
00:42:54,363 --> 00:42:56,822
<i>♪ Salutations to the One</i>
 <i>Worshipped by Lord Shiva Himself ♪</i>

456
00:42:56,863 --> 00:42:59,238
<i>♪ We worship You with all our hearts ♪</i>

457
00:42:59,280 --> 00:43:04,113
<i>♪ Salutations to Padmanabha</i>
 <i>Salutations to the soul of all existence ♪</i>

458
00:43:04,280 --> 00:43:06,697
<i>♪ Salutations to the One</i>
 <i>Worshipped by Lord Shiva Himself ♪</i>

459
00:43:06,863 --> 00:43:09,322
<i>♪ We worship You with all our hearts ♪</i>

460
00:43:29,447 --> 00:43:33,530
<i>♪ The gates of Vaikunta have opened ♪</i>

461
00:43:34,322 --> 00:43:36,780
<i>♪ The gates of Vaikunta have opened ♪</i>

462
00:43:39,113 --> 00:43:43,780
<i>♪ The gates of Vaikunta have opened</i>
 <i>The sacred Uttarayana season has arrived ♪</i>

463
00:43:43,988 --> 00:43:48,780
<i>♪ The chanting of the Ashtakshari mantra</i>
 <i>Bestows long life and prosperity ♪</i>

464
00:43:48,905 --> 00:43:53,697
<i>♪ Relieve the suffering</i>
 <i>And hardships of the poor ♪</i>

465
00:43:53,822 --> 00:43:58,488
<i>♪ Free them from the bondage</i>
 <i>Of their desires ♪</i>

466
00:43:58,738 --> 00:44:03,572
<i>♪ Strike down all calamity</i>
 <i>Like a divine weapon ♪</i>

467
00:44:03,655 --> 00:44:07,863
<i>♪ O Lord of Lords</i>
 <i>Shower Your mercy upon us ♪</i>

468
00:44:07,947 --> 00:44:12,655
<i>♪ Dweller of the sacred Vamana shrine</i>
 <i>O Srinivasa, guardian of the Kali Yuga ♪</i>

469
00:44:12,738 --> 00:44:17,905
<i>♪ We take refuge in You</i>
 <i>O Lord of Vaikunta ♪</i>

470
00:44:20,280 --> 00:44:25,030
<i>♪ Salutations to Padmanabha</i>
 <i>Salutations to the soul of all existence ♪</i>

471
00:44:25,113 --> 00:44:27,363
<i>♪ Salutations to the One</i>
 <i>Worshipped by Lord Shiva Himself ♪</i>

472
00:44:27,447 --> 00:44:29,780
<i>♪ We worship You with all our hearts ♪</i>

473
00:44:29,905 --> 00:44:34,613
<i>♪ Salutations to Padmanabha</i>
 <i>Salutations to the soul of all existence ♪</i>

474
00:44:34,738 --> 00:44:37,238
<i>♪ Salutations to the One</i>
 <i>Worshipped by Lord Shiva Himself ♪</i>

475
00:44:37,363 --> 00:44:40,155
<i>♪ We worship You with all our hearts ♪</i>

476
00:44:59,822 --> 00:45:06,363
<i>♪ Salutations to You, O Narayana ♪</i>

477
00:45:07,155 --> 00:45:13,030
<i>♪ Glory to You, O Hari ♪</i>

478
00:45:14,113 --> 00:45:18,905
<i>♪ O Narayana ♪</i>

479
00:45:19,405 --> 00:45:24,863
<i>♪ Glory to You, O Hari ♪</i>

480
00:48:48,530 --> 00:48:49,530
Robert!

481
00:50:45,572 --> 00:50:46,738
Sir, it's too risky.

482
00:50:47,572 --> 00:50:49,905
We can't go back. Keep going!

483
00:51:16,613 --> 00:51:18,238
-I've lost control.
-Take control!

484
00:51:18,405 --> 00:51:19,655
Hold on tight, sir.

485
00:51:19,822 --> 00:51:20,822
Hold on!

486
00:51:34,988 --> 00:51:36,072
I'm talking to you.

487
00:51:36,197 --> 00:51:38,613
I told you I don't want to go.
How many times must I say it?

488
00:51:38,738 --> 00:51:40,238
Raja doesn't listen
no matter what I say, brother.

489
00:51:40,572 --> 00:51:44,947
I went fishing for a small fish
and ended up with a whale.

490
00:51:45,113 --> 00:51:46,322
I told you to send them away.

491
00:51:46,822 --> 00:51:49,613
Hey Rudra, come on!

492
00:51:49,863 --> 00:51:53,030
-You're right on time.
-What's wrong, brother-in-law?

493
00:51:53,738 --> 00:51:55,280
No matter what I say,

494
00:51:55,363 --> 00:51:57,155
Gandhar Raju insists
I take them to Bhairavakona.

495
00:51:57,697 --> 00:51:59,863
We know well enough,
no one goes there and comes back.

496
00:52:00,197 --> 00:52:01,822
Some guy Shera
from Srirangapuram is here

497
00:52:01,947 --> 00:52:03,988
and he wants us
to take them there in our boat.

498
00:52:04,238 --> 00:52:06,988
They didn't come here asking for help,

499
00:52:07,613 --> 00:52:10,572
or demanding servitude.

500
00:52:10,738 --> 00:52:12,363
I brought these city folks here

501
00:52:12,405 --> 00:52:16,030
since they offered us some good money.

502
00:52:18,822 --> 00:52:21,738
Rudra, you can clear your debts.

503
00:52:22,030 --> 00:52:25,947
Your sister's wedding
can take place without a hitch.

504
00:52:38,238 --> 00:52:41,488
If money solves everything,
I'll take them.

505
00:52:42,863 --> 00:52:45,322
<i>We caught the big fish.</i>

506
00:52:45,863 --> 00:52:48,280
What are you saying?
Don't do this, Rudra!

507
00:52:48,905 --> 00:52:51,280
I don't know what Gandhara Raju
has in mind, brother-in-law.

508
00:52:51,780 --> 00:52:54,988
But all that's on my mind
is my sister's wedding.

509
00:53:30,530 --> 00:53:31,447
Hey!

510
00:53:31,697 --> 00:53:33,655
Why are you going to Bhairavakona?

511
00:53:36,280 --> 00:53:38,405
I'm asking you. What are we after?

512
00:53:40,280 --> 00:53:41,280
Well…

513
00:53:43,238 --> 00:53:46,738
that thing is as valuable
as it is dangerous.

514
00:53:47,613 --> 00:53:50,280
It's called… Sacred Lotus.

515
00:53:50,447 --> 00:53:51,655
What, a lotus?

516
00:53:53,322 --> 00:53:55,030
Someone like you wouldn't know its worth.

517
00:53:55,072 --> 00:53:58,863
Worth? Who risks their life
over a flower and some money?

518
00:53:59,197 --> 00:54:00,197
Come on, man.

519
00:54:00,988 --> 00:54:02,947
Hey, what's with your arrogance?

520
00:54:05,572 --> 00:54:06,988
I was born with it.

521
00:54:55,613 --> 00:54:56,738
What in the hell is this?

522
00:54:58,738 --> 00:55:00,738
Bhairavakona.

523
00:55:02,363 --> 00:55:03,738
Bhairavakona!

524
00:55:10,197 --> 00:55:11,988
Hey, keep moving forward.

525
00:55:12,697 --> 00:55:15,363
Anyone who goes ahead
never comes back.

526
00:55:18,113 --> 00:55:19,988
Why? Are you scared?

527
00:56:01,197 --> 00:56:03,363
-Let's move.
-Let's move.

528
00:56:26,405 --> 00:56:28,113
-Hey!
-They…

529
00:56:28,322 --> 00:56:30,530
are children of the forest, not beasts.

530
00:56:30,780 --> 00:56:31,697
-Leave.
-Hey!

531
00:56:59,988 --> 00:57:00,822
Hey!

532
00:57:17,947 --> 00:57:18,863
Hey!

533
00:57:31,780 --> 00:57:34,197
Anyone who stands in my way,

534
00:57:34,530 --> 00:57:36,655
I'll kill them. Even if it's you.

535
00:57:59,030 --> 00:57:59,988
Don't be afraid.

536
00:58:00,405 --> 00:58:02,697
Nothing will happen. It's only a sedative.

537
00:58:03,697 --> 00:58:05,238
What do you want anyway?

538
00:58:05,947 --> 00:58:06,905
The Sacred Lotus?

539
00:58:07,822 --> 00:58:10,655
No matter how hard it is, I'll bring it.

540
00:58:11,197 --> 00:58:11,905
What do you say?

541
00:58:36,530 --> 00:58:37,447
Let's hold it!

542
00:58:41,988 --> 00:58:43,655
Th-- The Sacred Lotus.

543
00:58:44,363 --> 00:58:45,530
It's aboard that flight.

544
00:58:49,363 --> 00:58:50,238
Will you go?

545
00:58:51,280 --> 00:58:52,447
You gave your word.

546
00:58:54,113 --> 00:58:55,197
Now, you go.

547
01:00:49,030 --> 01:00:50,447
Hey!

548
01:00:50,738 --> 01:00:52,072
Hey! Jump!

549
01:03:48,155 --> 01:03:50,030
Wake up! Wake up.

550
01:03:51,322 --> 01:03:53,655
-Brother. Please come here.
-Yes, dear.

551
01:03:54,113 --> 01:03:55,197
Please lend me a hand.

552
01:03:56,863 --> 01:03:59,405
-Hey, he's our Rudhra!
-Come on, help him.

553
01:05:37,447 --> 01:05:38,738
Can I ask you something?

554
01:05:42,280 --> 01:05:45,405
I saw you once
at the Srirangapuram festivities.

555
01:05:50,072 --> 01:05:52,447
You remembered me rather well,
for having seen me only once.

556
01:05:52,613 --> 01:05:56,405
How could I ever forget
the moment my life truly began?

557
01:06:03,072 --> 01:06:05,197
Did I say something wrong?

558
01:06:07,572 --> 01:06:08,405
No.

559
01:06:13,447 --> 01:06:14,572
Abdali!

560
01:06:14,863 --> 01:06:16,447
It was within reach,

561
01:06:16,822 --> 01:06:18,488
and then it slipped away, Bhairagi.

562
01:06:18,655 --> 01:06:22,155
It reached exactly
where it was meant to, Abdali.

563
01:06:22,697 --> 01:06:24,822
Such is the power of Time.

564
01:06:25,155 --> 01:06:27,822
Just as Time brought you to me,

565
01:06:28,197 --> 01:06:32,988
that Sacred Lotus
would have reached its destined place too.

566
01:06:33,822 --> 01:06:37,905
Many soldiers
must fall before a war is won.

567
01:06:38,447 --> 01:06:44,530
Then to obtain the Sacred Lotus
that rules the universe,

568
01:06:44,572 --> 01:06:46,488
how many more heads must roll?

569
01:06:47,322 --> 01:06:48,988
I'll be back, Bhairagi.

570
01:06:49,822 --> 01:06:51,030
Not alone.

571
01:06:52,155 --> 01:06:53,738
Along with the Sacred Lotus.

572
01:06:55,697 --> 01:06:56,988
Abdali!

573
01:06:57,822 --> 01:07:00,280
On the next full moon,

574
01:07:00,988 --> 01:07:04,447
the Sacred Lotus
will reach its peak power.

575
01:07:04,488 --> 01:07:09,863
Its energy will free me
from this Tree of Time.

576
01:07:09,988 --> 01:07:11,363
Remember!

577
01:07:11,447 --> 01:07:13,780
This is my last chance!

578
01:07:27,905 --> 01:07:28,988
She…

579
01:07:29,488 --> 01:07:33,447
She and Shera have been missing
since the night of the Brahmotsavam.

580
01:07:33,780 --> 01:07:35,905
Do you know why I really came here?

581
01:07:41,322 --> 01:07:45,072
Why is he frozen in place instead of
telling us how the Sacred Lotus was lost?

582
01:07:45,488 --> 01:07:49,363
Mr. Achyutachari, what is all this?
Why won't you say anything?

583
01:07:50,238 --> 01:07:53,322
What can he say?
What is there to say?

584
01:07:53,822 --> 01:07:56,072
He can neither evade responsibility,
not escape from here.

585
01:07:56,322 --> 01:07:59,197
Just as he's been swallowing
the Lord's offerings every day,

586
01:07:59,363 --> 01:08:02,280
he may well have stolen
the Sacred Lotus too.

587
01:08:02,447 --> 01:08:03,530
Sriranga!

588
01:08:08,238 --> 01:08:11,322
What are you all even saying?

589
01:08:12,572 --> 01:08:15,905
It is not right to suspect a man

590
01:08:16,613 --> 01:08:20,988
who has devoted his entire life
to this temple of being a thief.

591
01:08:21,447 --> 01:08:26,072
Mr. Sarathi, humiliating him like this
without knowing the truth is not right.

592
01:08:26,572 --> 01:08:29,363
Ma'am, it's not him
who's being humiliated.

593
01:08:29,613 --> 01:08:30,655
It is the temple's legacy.

594
01:08:30,947 --> 01:08:33,697
He has dishonored a heritage
preserved for generations.

595
01:08:33,988 --> 01:08:35,447
Why are you silent, Mr. Varma?

596
01:08:38,697 --> 01:08:42,488
Mr. Achyuta, what is all this?
Why won't you say anything?

597
01:08:45,197 --> 01:08:49,613
If it is obvious that he did it,
why would we care about his opinion?

598
01:08:49,822 --> 01:08:51,405
-Throw him out.
-Huh?

599
01:08:51,655 --> 01:08:53,238
-Get out!
-Dear.

600
01:08:54,113 --> 01:08:55,655
-What are you doing?
-[all] Get him out. Now!

601
01:08:55,822 --> 01:08:58,488
-Stop it!
-[all] Get lost!

602
01:09:00,947 --> 01:09:03,072
It is not for you
to decide right from wrong.

603
01:09:03,322 --> 01:09:04,238
Only God can.

604
01:09:06,030 --> 01:09:10,655
He says the Lord's feet are his home,
the Lord's service is his breath.

605
01:09:11,030 --> 01:09:16,197
He tends to the deity in the sanctum
like a child in its mother's womb.

606
01:09:17,280 --> 01:09:18,822
Why would he ever commit such a sin?

607
01:09:20,988 --> 01:09:23,905
If you all truly believe he did this,

608
01:09:24,613 --> 01:09:26,322
I will prove that

609
01:09:27,322 --> 01:09:30,697
you are wrong to suspect him,
and wrong to shame him!

610
01:09:32,280 --> 01:09:34,447
Wherever the Sacred Lotus may be…

611
01:09:35,072 --> 01:09:36,322
I will bring it back.

612
01:09:39,488 --> 01:09:41,405
The reason I was lying there, wounded…

613
01:09:42,613 --> 01:09:43,947
was because of the Sacred Lotus.

614
01:09:44,905 --> 01:09:48,572
-What? You saw the Sacred Lotus?
-Yeah.

615
01:09:48,863 --> 01:09:51,697
Where did you see it? Where is it now?

616
01:09:53,613 --> 01:09:54,905
-That…
-Rudra!

617
01:09:55,113 --> 01:09:56,572
-Brother. Brother.
-Rudra!

618
01:09:56,738 --> 01:09:57,947
-Brother-in-law!
-Mom!

619
01:09:58,155 --> 01:09:59,197
Rudra!

620
01:09:59,863 --> 01:10:02,530
Why did you go to Bhairavakona? Huh?

621
01:10:03,155 --> 01:10:04,280
What is this, brother?

622
01:10:04,697 --> 01:10:07,030
Why would you risk your life
for my wedding?

623
01:10:07,488 --> 01:10:09,405
What would happen to us
if anything happened to you?

624
01:10:09,572 --> 01:10:11,655
How did you stay away from me
for so many days?

625
01:10:11,863 --> 01:10:13,030
-Tell me.
-Hey, Manasa!

626
01:10:13,697 --> 01:10:15,405
Are you trying to put him back to sleep?

627
01:10:16,530 --> 01:10:18,905
I kept telling him, Aunt.
But would he listen to me?

628
01:10:20,447 --> 01:10:23,322
He risked his life believing
Gandhara Raja's deceptive words.

629
01:10:24,197 --> 01:10:28,322
If this girl hadn't arrived in time,
we would've lost our Rudra.

630
01:10:33,405 --> 01:10:35,530
You didn't save just one life, dear.

631
01:10:36,113 --> 01:10:37,238
You saved three.

632
01:10:38,488 --> 01:10:40,363
Not three. Four.

633
01:10:41,655 --> 01:10:42,530
Alright.

634
01:10:43,155 --> 01:10:44,488
What do you say, brother-in-law?

635
01:10:46,947 --> 01:10:48,947
-What is your name, dear?
-Parvathi.

636
01:10:50,822 --> 01:10:53,113
From now on, you are one of our family.

637
01:10:54,780 --> 01:10:57,363
Manasa's wedding is in two days.

638
01:10:58,238 --> 01:10:59,738
You must come.

639
01:11:09,030 --> 01:11:13,822
<i>♪ I'll give you stallions to ride</i>
 <i>And a kingdom to rule ♪</i>

640
01:11:14,113 --> 01:11:18,905
<i>♪ I'll give you stallions to ride</i>
 <i>And a kingdom to rule ♪</i>

641
01:11:19,072 --> 01:11:23,780
<i>♪ Come, O bridegroom</i>
 <i>Ascend the sacred dais ♪</i>

642
01:11:23,822 --> 01:11:28,780
<i>♪ Come, O bridegroom</i>
 <i>Ascend the sacred dais ♪</i>

643
01:11:29,197 --> 01:11:35,030
<i>♪ Come, O bridegroom</i>
 <i>Ascend the sacred dais ♪</i>

644
01:12:03,197 --> 01:12:06,655
<i>♪ Let the stars whirl and shine</i>
 <i>Hoy! Hoy! ♪</i>

645
01:12:06,697 --> 01:12:09,947
<i>♪ Let us raise festoons afar</i>
 <i>Hoy! Hoy! ♪</i>

646
01:12:10,072 --> 01:12:13,363
<i>♪ Slaughter the finest rams</i>
 <i>Hoy! Hoy! ♪</i>

647
01:12:13,530 --> 01:12:16,697
<i>♪ Cook the choicest goats</i>
 <i>Hoy! Hoy! ♪</i>

648
01:12:16,780 --> 01:12:19,988
<i>♪ The village has woven</i>
 <i>A silken bridal saree ♪</i>

649
01:12:20,113 --> 01:12:23,405
<i>♪ The goddess herself has sent</i>
 <i>Her blessings upon you ♪</i>

650
01:12:23,613 --> 01:12:26,947
<i>♪ The heavens descend</i>
 <i>To raise these wedding canopies ♪</i>

651
01:12:27,072 --> 01:12:30,197
<i>♪ Mother Earth herself</i>
 <i>Has laid this sacred altar ♪</i>

652
01:12:30,322 --> 01:12:33,947
<i>♪ Kith and kin gather</i>
 <i>To shower blessings upon you ♪</i>

653
01:12:33,988 --> 01:12:37,113
<i>♪ Let this wedding</i>
 <i>Be celebrated grandly ♪</i>

654
01:12:38,947 --> 01:12:42,405
<i>♪ Blow the sacred horn</i>
 <i>Proclaim it aloud ♪</i>

655
01:12:42,488 --> 01:12:45,780
<i>♪ Lift the bridal palanquin</i>
 <i>Hailo Hailessa ♪</i>

656
01:12:45,822 --> 01:12:49,280
<i>♪ Bring forth the feast</i>
 <i>From river and field ♪</i>

657
01:12:49,322 --> 01:12:52,697
<i>♪ Let joy whirl around</i>
 <i>Hailo Hailessa ♪</i>

658
01:13:54,447 --> 01:13:58,697
<i>♪ When he clasps my fingers</i>
 <i>My anklets softly chime ♪</i>

659
01:13:58,780 --> 01:14:02,947
<i>♪ My cheeks bloom red</i>
 <i>Like the Moduga flower ♪</i>

660
01:14:03,072 --> 01:14:06,405
<i>♪ Pearl-like grains adorn</i>
 <i>Her radiant face ♪</i>

661
01:14:06,447 --> 01:14:09,863
<i>♪ The groom shines like a gem</i>
 <i>Draped in silken grace ♪</i>

662
01:14:09,905 --> 01:14:16,405
<i>♪ The daughter raised with love</i>
 <i>Leaves her mother behind today ♪</i>

663
01:14:16,738 --> 01:14:20,947
<i>♪ When he clasps my fingers</i>
 <i>My anklets softly chime ♪</i>

664
01:14:21,030 --> 01:14:25,613
<i>♪ My cheeks bloom red</i>
 <i>Like the Moduga flower ♪</i>

665
01:14:27,280 --> 01:14:30,572
<i>♪ Your love overflows</i>
 <i>Like an endless river ♪</i>

666
01:14:30,655 --> 01:14:33,697
<i>♪ Protect us always</i>
 <i>O noble lord ♪</i>

667
01:14:34,113 --> 01:14:37,280
<i>♪ Like Ganga and Gowri</i>
 <i>We place our faith in you ♪</i>

668
01:14:37,322 --> 01:14:40,655
<i>♪ She crosses her village</i>
 <i>To belong to another home ♪</i>

669
01:14:40,738 --> 01:14:44,072
<i>♪ All our people pray</i>
 <i>She stays blessed with you ♪</i>

670
01:14:44,113 --> 01:14:47,572
<i>♪ Even if life demands sacrifice</i>
 <i>She remains my soul ♪</i>

671
01:14:47,655 --> 01:14:50,780
<i>♪ I swear upon</i>
 <i>The blood within me ♪</i>

672
01:14:50,822 --> 01:14:54,447
<i>♪ Wherever I may be</i>
 <i>I shall guard her in my heart ♪</i>

673
01:14:54,488 --> 01:14:58,238
<i>♪ I shall remain beside her</i>
 <i>Like a shadow ♪</i>

674
01:14:59,613 --> 01:15:03,030
<i>♪ Blow the sacred horn</i>
 <i>Proclaim it aloud ♪</i>

675
01:15:03,072 --> 01:15:06,197
<i>♪ Lift the bridal palanquin</i>
 <i>Hailo Hailessa ♪</i>

676
01:15:06,405 --> 01:15:09,863
<i>♪ Bring forth the feast</i>
 <i>From river and field ♪</i>

677
01:15:09,905 --> 01:15:13,238
<i>♪ Let joy whirl around</i>
 <i>Hailo Hailessa ♪</i>

678
01:15:59,780 --> 01:16:00,780
Raja!

679
01:16:03,238 --> 01:16:04,238
Raja!

680
01:16:24,572 --> 01:16:25,738
Dear!

681
01:16:32,072 --> 01:16:33,113
Dear!

682
01:16:36,613 --> 01:16:38,322
Raju! Raju!

683
01:16:41,197 --> 01:16:43,697
-Raja…
-Oh God!

684
01:16:48,697 --> 01:16:49,988
Oh no!

685
01:17:07,072 --> 01:17:08,322
Suvarna!

686
01:17:08,697 --> 01:17:12,030
You really wanted to get married, huh?

687
01:17:12,405 --> 01:17:14,238
You were meant to be in my bed.

688
01:17:14,322 --> 01:17:16,030
If you insist on being with him…

689
01:17:16,488 --> 01:17:19,280
do you think I'll let you? Come!

690
01:17:20,113 --> 01:17:22,697
You're making a mistake! Let her go!

691
01:17:23,780 --> 01:17:24,655
Sister!

692
01:17:25,030 --> 01:17:26,905
Hey! Let her go! I'm talking to yo--

693
01:17:29,530 --> 01:17:31,488
-Hey, he's your father!
-Hey!

694
01:17:32,905 --> 01:17:35,238
You watched while I was humiliated!

695
01:17:35,822 --> 01:17:38,072
You watched while hands were laid on me!

696
01:17:38,863 --> 01:17:41,197
You watched while my honor
was dragged through the streets!

697
01:17:41,780 --> 01:17:44,072
As a father, you've done nothing for me.

698
01:17:51,197 --> 01:17:54,738
Be it the man
who fathered me, or his wife…

699
01:17:55,363 --> 01:17:57,488
Whoever stands against me…

700
01:18:16,988 --> 01:18:22,405
After all this time, I finally see
my family truly is and who isn't.

701
01:18:25,322 --> 01:18:26,863
I'm telling you, as your aunt.

702
01:18:29,155 --> 01:18:30,738
Hack him down, Rudra!

703
01:19:42,697 --> 01:19:44,905
There's the bugger you wanted.

704
01:19:46,113 --> 01:19:47,072
Hey, Rudra!

705
01:19:47,655 --> 01:19:51,488
I thought you'd die
that day in Bhairavakona.

706
01:19:51,947 --> 01:19:54,655
But today…
Even if the Goddess herself descends,

707
01:19:54,822 --> 01:19:57,572
she cannot save you or your family!

708
01:19:57,988 --> 01:19:58,947
Nephew!

709
01:19:59,947 --> 01:20:01,447
Drag her here!

710
01:21:56,113 --> 01:21:58,613
Hey! Bind him up!

711
01:22:02,738 --> 01:22:04,530
-Rudra!
-Brother!

712
01:22:10,697 --> 01:22:11,822
Rudra!

713
01:22:12,863 --> 01:22:15,697
Rudra! He's no ordinary man!

714
01:22:15,822 --> 01:22:18,572
-A demon! You saw it yourself.
-It's the truth.

715
01:22:18,988 --> 01:22:21,905
He turned your village
into a sea of blood.

716
01:22:21,947 --> 01:22:23,030
-No!
-Listen to me.

717
01:22:23,238 --> 01:22:25,030
Tell me where the Sacred Lotus is!

718
01:22:25,072 --> 01:22:25,947
Speak!

719
01:22:25,988 --> 01:22:28,072
Had I known,
I'd have brought it long ago!

720
01:22:28,113 --> 01:22:29,655
This won't make him speak.

721
01:22:29,738 --> 01:22:31,863
Stab him! That'll do it!

722
01:22:32,947 --> 01:22:34,530
-Brother-in law!
-Hey!

723
01:22:35,738 --> 01:22:37,613
Rudra! Rudra!

724
01:22:37,738 --> 01:22:41,322
Someone save him! Oh, God!

725
01:22:41,530 --> 01:22:43,905
-Do you want me to kill them all?
-My--

726
01:22:46,780 --> 01:22:50,030
-Oh, dear!
-My love--

727
01:23:03,363 --> 01:23:04,322
Hey!

728
01:23:12,530 --> 01:23:13,363
Mother!

729
01:23:13,488 --> 01:23:18,113
How can you just stand there
like a statue after seeing all this?

730
01:23:20,280 --> 01:23:21,405
Alas!

731
01:23:21,655 --> 01:23:22,822
Stop!

732
01:23:23,072 --> 01:23:24,905
You think you are
a great devotee like Prahlada?

733
01:23:25,822 --> 01:23:28,780
Call upon your savior then!

734
01:23:30,822 --> 01:23:31,988
Let me see!

735
01:23:32,530 --> 01:23:33,905
Hey!

736
01:23:34,822 --> 01:23:36,905
-No!
-Leave her!

737
01:23:37,863 --> 01:23:39,780
Mother!

738
01:23:51,488 --> 01:23:52,447
Anyway…

739
01:23:53,363 --> 01:23:56,113
For the Lord to descend on earth…

740
01:23:56,822 --> 01:23:58,988
This is not the era of Kalki…

741
01:24:00,363 --> 01:24:01,363
It's Kali's era!

742
01:24:02,780 --> 01:24:03,780
My era!

743
01:24:13,238 --> 01:24:15,197
No matter how many births I take…

744
01:24:15,905 --> 01:24:17,530
It is all for my own desire.

745
01:24:18,905 --> 01:24:22,655
Until my wish is fulfilled…
I shall keep returning.

746
01:24:23,322 --> 01:24:25,905
What will make you
handover the Sacred Lotus?

747
01:24:25,947 --> 01:24:28,488
No matter how many lives you take…

748
01:24:29,113 --> 01:24:32,822
The truth will never leave his lips, sir.

749
01:24:32,988 --> 01:24:35,655
Like the sorcerer's life
hidden in a parrot…

750
01:24:35,697 --> 01:24:38,238
His life rests within that bird.

751
01:24:43,780 --> 01:24:46,780
-<i>♪ I'll give you stallions to ride ♪</i>
-Hey!

752
01:24:49,613 --> 01:24:50,572
Hey!

753
01:24:53,488 --> 01:24:55,655
-Hey! Leave my sister!
-Please let Manasa go.

754
01:24:55,738 --> 01:24:58,447
Your sister is your very life, is she not?

755
01:24:59,488 --> 01:25:03,905
Will you speak now or shall I kill her?

756
01:25:08,530 --> 01:25:09,947
Brother!

757
01:25:18,322 --> 01:25:19,322
Hey!

758
01:25:23,697 --> 01:25:24,988
Brother!

759
01:26:07,280 --> 01:26:08,822
<i>Brother!</i>

760
01:27:34,197 --> 01:27:35,030
Hey.

761
01:27:49,822 --> 01:27:50,780
Kill him!

762
01:28:12,905 --> 01:28:13,738
Hey!

763
01:30:57,655 --> 01:31:03,238
<i>♪ Are You there or not, O Eshwara? ♪</i>

764
01:31:04,280 --> 01:31:10,572
<i>♪ If You are, what divine drama? ♪</i>

765
01:31:10,697 --> 01:31:16,947
<i>♪ You are a God who cannot guard or save ♪</i>

766
01:31:17,113 --> 01:31:23,280
<i>♪ Is all this sin</i>
 <i>Your share to brave? ♪</i>

767
01:31:23,405 --> 01:31:30,155
<i>♪ For us</i>
 <i>Is birth itself a chain, a curse? ♪</i>

768
01:31:30,363 --> 01:31:34,613
<i>♪ O Eshwara ♪</i>

769
01:31:36,697 --> 01:31:39,780
<i>-♪ For You, is the funeral fire ♪</i>
-Hey, wait!

770
01:31:40,405 --> 01:31:43,488
<i>♪ Salvation's verse? ♪</i>

771
01:31:43,655 --> 01:31:46,947
<i>♪ O Eternal One ♪</i>

772
01:31:49,780 --> 01:31:53,572
<i>♪ Time itself… ♪</i>

773
01:32:01,488 --> 01:32:08,030
<i>-My life.</i>
 <i>-♪ Like poison fell ♪</i>

774
01:32:09,238 --> 01:32:10,197
Sister!

775
01:32:16,030 --> 01:32:22,405
<i>♪ Time itself, like poison fell</i>
 <i>Carving wounds so deep ♪</i>

776
01:32:22,530 --> 01:32:29,155
<i>♪ Silence turned a lullaby</i>
 <i>Asking me no reply to keep ♪</i>

777
01:32:29,238 --> 01:32:32,405
<i>♪ Time itself like poison fell ♪</i>

778
01:32:32,530 --> 01:32:35,655
<i>♪ Carving wounds so deep ♪</i>

779
01:32:35,738 --> 01:32:42,863
<i>♪ Silence turned a lullaby</i>
 <i>Asking me no reply to keep ♪</i>

780
01:32:57,447 --> 01:32:58,572
<i>What do you say?</i>

781
01:32:58,738 --> 01:33:00,197
<i>My love--</i>

782
01:33:08,905 --> 01:33:12,030
<i>♪ Eshwara! ♪</i>

783
01:33:13,280 --> 01:33:17,363
<i>♪ Eshwara! ♪</i>

784
01:33:47,738 --> 01:33:49,238
Hey, Shiva!

785
01:33:49,572 --> 01:33:50,988
My name isn't Shiva.

786
01:33:51,988 --> 01:33:52,947
It's Rudra!

787
01:33:53,613 --> 01:33:55,113
They're both the same.

788
01:33:55,363 --> 01:33:58,488
When he lets go, he's Rudra.
When he embraces, he's Shiva.

789
01:33:58,655 --> 01:34:00,155
That's the only difference.

790
01:34:01,238 --> 01:34:04,113
What is it? Thinking too much?

791
01:34:04,488 --> 01:34:05,947
Or drowning in sorrow?

792
01:34:08,405 --> 01:34:11,030
When your dreams burn
before your eyes,

793
01:34:11,488 --> 01:34:13,447
faith begins to slip away.

794
01:34:13,613 --> 01:34:17,405
Only the one who holds on tight
can keep from falling apart.

795
01:34:17,530 --> 01:34:21,155
Swami, death is what gives beauty to life.

796
01:34:21,322 --> 01:34:26,530
But man fails to understand that
and keeps chasing worldly attachments.

797
01:34:29,280 --> 01:34:31,488
He grants nine months for birth

798
01:34:31,863 --> 01:34:34,613
but he can snatch it away in an instant.

799
01:34:35,113 --> 01:34:36,947
Have you ever wondered why?

800
01:34:37,155 --> 01:34:40,572
Because if death came with a warning,

801
01:34:40,655 --> 01:34:44,322
man would spend his whole life
destroying himself in fear.

802
01:34:45,030 --> 01:34:46,572
That's what I'm afraid of.

803
01:34:47,030 --> 01:34:48,113
Swami!

804
01:34:49,280 --> 01:34:52,072
Life is about moving forward
while holding onto memories

805
01:34:53,030 --> 01:34:57,238
of the departed and searching
for unanswered questions!

806
01:34:57,947 --> 01:34:59,072
Swami!

807
01:34:59,488 --> 01:35:02,447
Even Shiva himself, smeared in sacred ash,

808
01:35:03,030 --> 01:35:08,488
he didn't perish with his beloved
when he lost her to the flames, Swami.

809
01:35:10,322 --> 01:35:13,613
He sought the reason behind it
and destroyed everyone responsible.

810
01:35:15,988 --> 01:35:19,572
"I don't want this war! I won't fight it!"

811
01:35:19,738 --> 01:35:22,655
When Arjuna tried
to walk away in detachment…

812
01:35:24,738 --> 01:35:27,572
didn't Lord Krishna
bring him back to Kurukshetra?

813
01:35:29,488 --> 01:35:31,613
What you do for yourself is duty.

814
01:35:32,238 --> 01:35:34,488
What you do for others is righteousness.

815
01:35:35,155 --> 01:35:38,988
Grieving endlessly
over the dead is futile.

816
01:35:39,572 --> 01:35:43,155
Because you came into this world alone,

817
01:35:43,405 --> 01:35:45,280
and you'll leave it alone too.

818
01:35:46,655 --> 01:35:47,572
Swami.

819
01:35:48,030 --> 01:35:50,405
Do you know
what truly lasts forever in this world?

820
01:35:52,322 --> 01:35:54,363
Truth shall be your mother,

821
01:35:55,030 --> 01:35:57,238
wisdom your father,

822
01:35:57,530 --> 01:35:59,613
righteousness is your sibling,

823
01:35:59,947 --> 01:36:01,905
compassion is your friend,

824
01:36:02,155 --> 01:36:04,155
peace is your wife

825
01:36:04,447 --> 01:36:06,738
and forgiveness is your child.

826
01:36:09,030 --> 01:36:10,572
Only these six are eternal.

827
01:36:11,072 --> 01:36:13,863
Everything else is temporary.

828
01:36:20,072 --> 01:36:23,322
Time will tell you why you were born.

829
01:36:24,613 --> 01:36:28,613
But only you can discover
the meaning of your birth.

830
01:36:29,863 --> 01:36:30,863
You'll find it.

831
01:36:32,197 --> 01:36:35,697
Rudra… you'll find your path.

832
01:36:36,205 --> 01:36:36,757
Yeah.

833
01:36:39,738 --> 01:36:45,197
<i>♪ Lord of Ashes, O Linga</i>
 <i>What is this divine play of yours? ♪</i>

834
01:36:50,197 --> 01:36:51,030
<i>Parvathi.</i>

835
01:36:53,447 --> 01:36:55,447
<i>Do you know why I'm actually here?</i>

836
01:36:57,863 --> 01:37:00,405
<i>-The Sacred Lotus…</i>
 <i>-Tell me where it is.</i>

837
01:37:06,280 --> 01:37:09,447
<i>-It is known as Sacred Lotus.</i>
 <i>-Some guy from town named Shera.</i>

838
01:37:12,613 --> 01:37:14,155
<i>You'll find your path.</i>

839
01:37:15,697 --> 01:37:17,405
<i>Have you seen the Sacred Lotus?</i>

840
01:37:19,405 --> 01:37:21,488
<i>She and Shera are missing.</i>

841
01:38:06,572 --> 01:38:08,530
Poor soul. How did he die?

842
01:38:08,947 --> 01:38:13,072
He falsely accused Achyutachari,
who had done nothing wrong.

843
01:38:13,197 --> 01:38:14,197
He's gone.

844
01:38:25,988 --> 01:38:29,530
-I knew you would come.
-They destroyed our entire settlement.

845
01:38:30,238 --> 01:38:32,988
They took away everyone
I ever called my own.

846
01:38:33,780 --> 01:38:35,363
They reduced our lives to ashes.

847
01:38:36,572 --> 01:38:38,072
All for that Sacred Lotus…

848
01:38:41,030 --> 01:38:44,947
They killed my sister
under a wedding canopy.

849
01:38:48,488 --> 01:38:50,238
They turned my mother into a corpse.

850
01:38:52,988 --> 01:38:56,280
They drowned the entire village
in blood, even innocent children.

851
01:38:57,572 --> 01:38:58,530
Mom!

852
01:38:58,947 --> 01:39:01,488
What's your connection to Shera,
the man behind this massacre?

853
01:39:02,322 --> 01:39:05,988
We have… nothing to do with Shera.

854
01:39:08,738 --> 01:39:10,488
The reason behind all this…

855
01:39:24,822 --> 01:39:26,447
Their arrival that day…

856
01:39:27,072 --> 01:39:31,072
ruined our lives
and disgraced our lineage.

857
01:39:32,030 --> 01:39:34,530
You're not asking for help to do good.

858
01:39:35,322 --> 01:39:37,655
You're asking me to aid a wrongdoing.

859
01:39:38,238 --> 01:39:40,655
That will never happen,
even if I lose my life.

860
01:39:51,238 --> 01:39:52,697
Ravi Varma…

861
01:39:54,197 --> 01:39:57,322
You may set and rise again, like the sun.

862
01:39:59,280 --> 01:40:01,530
But your bloodline… your children…

863
01:40:02,447 --> 01:40:04,322
once they perish…

864
01:40:05,780 --> 01:40:07,405
they'll never rise again.

865
01:40:11,863 --> 01:40:14,905
Anyone can bring the temple key.

866
01:40:15,238 --> 01:40:19,363
But only Achyutachari
can open the temple doors.

867
01:40:20,155 --> 01:40:22,363
Achyuta? Who is he?

868
01:40:23,072 --> 01:40:26,863
He's the temple's chief priest.
Only he knows the secret.

869
01:40:26,947 --> 01:40:30,238
Not even the fear of death
could make him speak.

870
01:40:31,363 --> 01:40:35,572
-Then how do we make him talk?
-Earn his trust.

871
01:40:37,530 --> 01:40:39,613
Trust cuts deeper than fear.

872
01:40:41,488 --> 01:40:42,738
Make him trust you.

873
01:40:45,447 --> 01:40:47,030
As part of the plan,

874
01:40:47,405 --> 01:40:51,280
Parvathi entered Achyutachari's family.

875
01:40:51,988 --> 01:40:55,530
She got close to them
and earned everyone's trust.

876
01:40:56,280 --> 01:41:00,155
To keep themselves informed
of every event…

877
01:41:01,363 --> 01:41:03,113
They sent Shera to us.

878
01:41:05,530 --> 01:41:09,822
Parvati, having uncovered the secret
of the lock that no one else knew,

879
01:41:10,072 --> 01:41:12,197
on the final night of the festivities…

880
01:41:45,947 --> 01:41:47,072
But

881
01:41:47,572 --> 01:41:49,863
carrying a god is
easier than…

882
01:41:51,337 --> 01:41:52,337
stealing one.

883
01:41:55,822 --> 01:41:57,447
-Hello.<i>-Ravi Varma.</i>

884
01:41:57,572 --> 01:41:59,488
<i>The plane crashed near Bhairavakona.</i>

885
01:42:00,238 --> 01:42:02,072
<i>The Sacred Lotus</i>
 <i>remains inside the wreckage.</i>

886
01:42:02,280 --> 01:42:03,822
<i>Tell Parvathi immediately.</i>

887
01:42:07,822 --> 01:42:09,613
It was for that Sacred Lotus

888
01:42:09,738 --> 01:42:12,947
that Parvathi and Shera
came to your hamlet.

889
01:42:23,072 --> 01:42:25,238
I don't know what happened

890
01:42:25,447 --> 01:42:28,822
after Parvathi and Shera
reached your village.

891
01:42:29,530 --> 01:42:30,232
But,

892
01:42:32,822 --> 01:42:34,863
if you want to know the whole truth

893
01:42:35,405 --> 01:42:37,530
you must first find Parvathi.

894
01:42:44,238 --> 01:42:46,363
Go straight and turn right.

895
01:43:17,988 --> 01:43:18,947
Guruji!

896
01:43:21,863 --> 01:43:23,072
Parvathi, my dear!

897
01:43:23,363 --> 01:43:25,655
What happened? Tell me!

898
01:43:29,447 --> 01:43:32,030
-Forgive me, Guruji.
-What happened, child?

899
01:43:33,113 --> 01:43:35,738
-What happened?
-I must tell you the truth.

900
01:43:37,988 --> 01:43:42,197
The one who stole the Sacred Lotus
was none other than… me.

901
01:43:46,530 --> 01:43:50,280
You'd have heard
tales of demons in legends

902
01:43:50,822 --> 01:43:52,488
and read about them in books.

903
01:43:53,530 --> 01:43:56,280
But I saw one with my own eyes.

904
01:43:57,822 --> 01:44:00,697
That demon is Zulfiqar Ali.

905
01:44:02,030 --> 01:44:04,780
It was because of him
that I committed this terrible act.

906
01:44:05,447 --> 01:44:07,447
I never did it willingly, Guruji.

907
01:44:08,697 --> 01:44:09,988
Please forgive me.

908
01:44:10,863 --> 01:44:12,238
Please forgive me.

909
01:44:15,113 --> 01:44:18,572
Mr. Prabhakar,
the Indian Archaeology Department Chief…

910
01:44:19,613 --> 01:44:20,530
was my father.

911
01:44:22,738 --> 01:44:25,988
My sister Revathi, Tesla,
and Zulfiqar Ali…

912
01:44:26,530 --> 01:44:28,863
were all archaeology students together.

913
01:44:32,030 --> 01:44:35,363
My sister and Tesla
fell in love with each other.

914
01:44:39,447 --> 01:44:42,697
Since Tesla is a Britisher,
my father didn't approve.

915
01:44:43,988 --> 01:44:48,322
So they got married
without his knowledge.

916
01:44:54,030 --> 01:44:56,072
-Yeah, sure. Hi, Parvathi.
-Stop!

917
01:44:59,030 --> 01:45:00,780
You married against my wishes.

918
01:45:01,322 --> 01:45:02,655
Go wherever you please.

919
01:45:08,947 --> 01:45:09,572
Sister!

920
01:45:12,405 --> 01:45:14,405
Unable to forget what my sister did,

921
01:45:14,655 --> 01:45:18,697
father stopped going to work
and shut himself away in grief.

922
01:45:19,030 --> 01:45:20,863
-Some time later…
-[phone rings]

923
01:45:20,988 --> 01:45:21,822
What?!

924
01:45:23,322 --> 01:45:26,238
Congratulations! Are you serious?

925
01:45:27,322 --> 01:45:29,947
Dad! you're going to be a granddad.

926
01:45:32,113 --> 01:45:34,322
The moment he learned he had
a granddaughter,

927
01:45:34,530 --> 01:45:36,655
he invited them home.

928
01:45:38,655 --> 01:45:39,697
Grandpa!

929
01:45:39,780 --> 01:45:42,697
After that, Riya became his whole world.

930
01:45:44,947 --> 01:45:46,072
Grandpa!

931
01:46:01,113 --> 01:46:03,863
My father's love for Riya grew stronger,

932
01:46:04,363 --> 01:46:06,572
but his anger toward
Tesla never faded.

933
01:46:07,072 --> 01:46:08,530
Driven by that anger,

934
01:46:08,822 --> 01:46:12,822
my father entrusted Ali with finding
the Temple of the Virata Purusha

935
01:46:13,072 --> 01:46:14,738
and asked him to assist Tesla.

936
01:46:15,072 --> 01:46:18,780
Tesla found the Nagabandham scripture
during that research.

937
01:46:19,113 --> 01:46:22,447
Realizing Ali would come
for the Nagabandham scripture at any cost…

938
01:46:22,613 --> 01:46:24,905
Sir, I only trust you.

939
01:46:26,613 --> 01:46:28,655
India's future is in your hands.

940
01:46:34,405 --> 01:46:36,780
Please let us go, Uncle!

941
01:46:43,363 --> 01:46:45,113
Daddy!

942
01:46:46,363 --> 01:46:47,322
Daddy!

943
01:46:47,405 --> 01:46:49,530
-Riya, my dear…
-Grandpa!

944
01:46:49,822 --> 01:46:51,447
-Come here.
-Grandpa.

945
01:46:53,905 --> 01:46:56,030
Grandpa… Mommy!

946
01:46:58,405 --> 01:46:59,863
Mommy…

947
01:47:02,447 --> 01:47:05,197
Grandpa, he hit mommy.

948
01:47:05,947 --> 01:47:07,447
-Revathi!
-Mommy.

949
01:47:07,530 --> 01:47:09,072
Robert! Revathi!

950
01:47:12,447 --> 01:47:14,863
Robert! Hey! Hey!

951
01:47:15,405 --> 01:47:17,530
-Revathi…
-Dad! Dad!

952
01:47:17,863 --> 01:47:19,238
Rev-- Revathi!

953
01:47:19,488 --> 01:47:22,488
-Revathi! You…
-What kind of people are you?

954
01:47:23,197 --> 01:47:27,655
You never showed this love
while they were alive.

955
01:47:28,822 --> 01:47:30,655
Did it appear only after they died?!

956
01:47:31,072 --> 01:47:31,988
Hey!

957
01:47:36,030 --> 01:47:38,530
This is the book you wanted, right?

958
01:47:42,030 --> 01:47:44,655
Take it and let my Grandpa go.

959
01:47:45,197 --> 01:47:48,280
Please, Uncle. Let us go.

960
01:47:56,530 --> 01:47:58,405
-Revathi, my child!
-Dad!

961
01:48:00,030 --> 01:48:03,530
-You won't have to be angry anymore…
-No.

962
01:48:05,363 --> 01:48:07,488
I won't be there either.

963
01:48:08,113 --> 01:48:09,988
Dear Revathi!

964
01:48:10,155 --> 01:48:12,447
My baby… Ba--

965
01:48:12,988 --> 01:48:16,113
-Take… care of her, Dad.
-Don't say that.

966
01:48:16,988 --> 01:48:19,738
-Mommy! Mommy!
-Revathi.

967
01:48:19,905 --> 01:48:22,947
-Revathi, my child!
-Mommy! No!

968
01:48:24,988 --> 01:48:26,113
Hey, Ali!

969
01:48:26,947 --> 01:48:29,363
If the Serpent seal
is like a Lotus formation,

970
01:48:30,322 --> 01:48:33,988
the scripture in your hand is
an Abhimanyu!

971
01:48:35,113 --> 01:48:38,280
It will only show you the way in!

972
01:48:42,905 --> 01:48:44,863
Grandpa!

973
01:48:48,072 --> 01:48:52,030
So… you're the solution
to find my way back.

974
01:48:54,863 --> 01:48:55,905
Later on,

975
01:48:56,238 --> 01:48:58,572
my father found out that Sacred Lotus

976
01:48:58,780 --> 01:49:01,697
is in Srirangapuram
through Nagabandham scripture.

977
01:49:02,197 --> 01:49:03,405
But…

978
01:49:03,988 --> 01:49:05,863
my conscience wouldn't allow me…

979
01:49:07,530 --> 01:49:09,530
to steal the Sacred Lotus.

980
01:49:12,447 --> 01:49:14,113
At that moment…

981
01:49:28,322 --> 01:49:30,197
Riya!
Riya!

982
01:49:33,530 --> 01:49:35,613
Bringing it here isn't that easy.

983
01:49:35,947 --> 01:49:36,780
And Riya?

984
01:49:40,822 --> 01:49:42,488
She misses you a lot.

985
01:49:43,905 --> 01:49:46,113
The longer you delay,
the greater the danger.

986
01:49:55,738 --> 01:49:56,655
Dad…

987
01:49:57,197 --> 01:49:59,905
this isn't just wrong… it's a sin.

988
01:50:00,947 --> 01:50:02,947
I don't know where this will lead us.

989
01:50:03,613 --> 01:50:05,113
When something becomes unavoidable,

990
01:50:05,738 --> 01:50:08,447
we can't think about right and wrong.

991
01:50:10,155 --> 01:50:11,738
When the intention is pure,

992
01:50:12,780 --> 01:50:15,655
one who accepts
even poison as nectar is God.

993
01:50:17,280 --> 01:50:18,947
He will understand.

994
01:50:22,613 --> 01:50:25,655
Even asking for forgiveness
feels like a grave sin now.

995
01:50:27,155 --> 01:50:31,697
We desecrated a sacred temple
for our own selfish needs.

996
01:50:33,780 --> 01:50:37,072
-And I framed you for it.
-You should be killed.

997
01:50:40,280 --> 01:50:43,363
-Rudra?
-You drove him away from the temple.

998
01:50:43,905 --> 01:50:46,322
You took away everyone I had.

999
01:50:47,155 --> 01:50:48,238
Rudra!

1000
01:50:49,905 --> 01:50:52,655
I had nothing to do
with that massacre, Rudra.

1001
01:50:52,822 --> 01:50:55,863
I came to your village
only for the Sacred Lotus.

1002
01:50:56,780 --> 01:50:58,155
And I met you.

1003
01:50:58,822 --> 01:51:01,905
That day, no one who went
after the Sacred Lotus returned.

1004
01:51:02,447 --> 01:51:05,113
But I found you
lying injured on the shore.

1005
01:51:05,405 --> 01:51:07,863
I searched you,
thinking you might have it.

1006
01:51:07,988 --> 01:51:08,988
But it wasn't there.

1007
01:51:09,363 --> 01:51:11,530
You were the only one
who knew anything about it.

1008
01:51:11,947 --> 01:51:13,238
That's why I saved you.

1009
01:51:13,738 --> 01:51:17,447
I tried many times to ask you about it
after you regained consciousness.

1010
01:51:18,572 --> 01:51:21,197
But before that could happen
the tragedy unfolded.

1011
01:51:21,572 --> 01:51:22,905
Why have you come now?

1012
01:51:28,322 --> 01:51:30,322
We brought
you the Sacred Lotus you wanted.

1013
01:51:30,822 --> 01:51:33,780
Where is our Riya?
Return my granddaughter to me.

1014
01:51:37,072 --> 01:51:38,947
It's not over yet, Prabhakar.

1015
01:51:39,280 --> 01:51:41,155
There's one small task left.

1016
01:51:41,613 --> 01:51:43,905
What else is left now except destruction?

1017
01:51:47,155 --> 01:51:50,572
The very land I once walked with pride,

1018
01:51:52,197 --> 01:51:54,947
the culture I spoke of with honor,

1019
01:51:55,488 --> 01:51:58,447
you made me betray that very soil.

1020
01:51:58,697 --> 01:51:59,738
Hey!

1021
01:51:59,905 --> 01:52:01,697
You burned down the village,

1022
01:52:02,780 --> 01:52:04,655
and slaughtered innocent people.

1023
01:52:06,780 --> 01:52:09,905
Using a little girl's life as leverage,

1024
01:52:10,613 --> 01:52:14,447
you turned a patriot into a traitor.

1025
01:52:15,113 --> 01:52:17,238
What more is left now?

1026
01:52:17,322 --> 01:52:19,197
Tell me! What else is left?!

1027
01:52:19,530 --> 01:52:22,113
-What else?!
-Ali…

1028
01:52:22,447 --> 01:52:25,697
Please let us go.
We can't endure this anymore.

1029
01:52:25,863 --> 01:52:27,655
Kill both of us if you want!

1030
01:52:27,947 --> 01:52:29,905
But please spare Riya.

1031
01:52:30,322 --> 01:52:32,363
Ever since we obeyed you,

1032
01:52:32,488 --> 01:52:38,030
every moment of our lives
has felt like breathing poison.

1033
01:52:39,572 --> 01:52:42,030
After witnessing so much betrayal
and so many deaths…

1034
01:52:42,155 --> 01:52:44,863
What is even left for us to live for?

1035
01:52:44,947 --> 01:52:48,530
We can't take this anymore.
Show us some mercy.

1036
01:52:50,113 --> 01:52:52,738
There's only one thing
this Abdali doesn't know.

1037
01:52:53,363 --> 01:52:54,947
Mercy.

1038
01:52:57,197 --> 01:52:58,863
I need one final thing from you.

1039
01:52:59,363 --> 01:53:01,530
Please understand.

1040
01:53:02,447 --> 01:53:03,863
He wants the Garuda mantras!

1041
01:53:04,697 --> 01:53:07,322
We'll stay alive
only if we hand them over to Ali.

1042
01:53:11,530 --> 01:53:13,488
Only you can save us, Guruji.

1043
01:53:32,988 --> 01:53:35,530
Salutations to Shiva and Vishnu
each the reflection of the other.

1044
01:53:37,197 --> 01:53:39,072
Our ancestors used to say
that along with the Sacred Lotus,

1045
01:53:39,655 --> 01:53:43,322
these palm-leaf scriptures,
were also entrusted to us by sages.

1046
01:53:43,863 --> 01:53:46,447
I believe you alone
will restore the Sacred Lotus,

1047
01:53:47,363 --> 01:53:49,947
to Lord Ranganatha's navel, son.

1048
01:53:51,280 --> 01:53:52,238
Here.

1049
01:53:57,072 --> 01:53:58,280
May victory be yours.

1050
01:54:02,488 --> 01:54:04,113
Bhairagi!

1051
01:56:26,655 --> 01:56:27,738
Leave me!

1052
01:56:29,363 --> 01:56:30,405
Grandpa!

1053
01:56:31,572 --> 01:56:32,447
Riya!

1054
01:56:32,988 --> 01:56:35,447
-My dear Riya!
-Grandpa!

1055
01:56:36,488 --> 01:56:38,197
-Riya!
-Grandpa!

1056
01:56:38,405 --> 01:56:39,613
Riya!

1057
01:56:40,447 --> 01:56:42,113
Dear Riya!

1058
01:57:45,447 --> 01:57:48,072
The Serpent seal is being unlocked!

1059
01:57:49,780 --> 01:57:51,613
A dream I cherished for years…

1060
01:57:53,238 --> 01:57:56,197
is finally becoming reality today.

1061
01:57:58,613 --> 01:57:59,988
Abdali!

1062
01:58:01,405 --> 01:58:04,238
The time to rule the universe

1063
01:58:05,405 --> 01:58:07,072
is drawing near.

1064
01:58:09,197 --> 01:58:12,113
The eclipse full moon is approaching.

1065
01:58:12,863 --> 01:58:15,530
The Serpent seal will be unlocked!

1066
01:58:18,697 --> 01:58:20,697
Now all that's left,

1067
01:58:21,822 --> 01:58:24,447
is to get my hands on the Garuda mantras.

1068
01:58:24,822 --> 01:58:27,488
Soon they'll be in your hands, Bhairagi.

1069
01:58:28,530 --> 01:58:30,363
Once the Garuda mantras arrive,

1070
01:58:30,947 --> 01:58:35,697
you reciting them will open
the Serpent sealed gate,

1071
01:58:35,822 --> 01:58:37,280
and we'll step inside…

1072
01:58:37,447 --> 01:58:39,863
everything will happen
as planned, Bhairagi.

1073
01:58:43,113 --> 01:58:44,072
Fool!

1074
01:58:48,113 --> 01:58:51,363
To protect righteousness, in every age,

1075
01:58:51,988 --> 01:58:54,030
in whatever form he must take,

1076
01:58:55,947 --> 01:58:58,530
however many times he must be reborn,

1077
01:58:59,947 --> 01:59:01,822
the Lord will always return.

1078
01:59:03,947 --> 01:59:05,780
And he will stop demons like you

1079
01:59:06,488 --> 01:59:09,363
from entering that divine gateway.

1080
01:59:12,697 --> 01:59:15,613
Kali controls the Time now, Prabhakar.

1081
01:59:16,155 --> 01:59:19,780
No one can stop our mission anymore.

1082
01:59:20,238 --> 01:59:21,405
No one is coming.

1083
01:59:26,655 --> 01:59:27,988
Grandpa!

1084
01:59:31,530 --> 01:59:33,530
Grandpa!

1085
02:00:02,155 --> 02:00:03,780
Aunt!

1086
02:00:03,988 --> 02:00:05,905
Grandpa!

1087
02:00:06,447 --> 02:00:07,322
Riya!

1088
02:00:31,530 --> 02:00:33,447
Dad! Dad!

1089
02:00:34,322 --> 02:00:36,947
Grandpa, please!

1090
02:00:37,280 --> 02:00:38,447
Dad…

1091
02:01:01,465 --> 02:01:03,173
Hey!

1092
02:01:38,947 --> 02:01:41,238
Shiva!

1093
02:02:24,447 --> 02:02:25,322
Please, come.

1094
02:02:29,280 --> 02:02:31,238
-Greetings.
-Greetings, Swami.

1095
02:02:31,447 --> 02:02:33,613
What do you have
in your hands, little one?

1096
02:02:33,655 --> 02:02:36,280
A Tulasi garland for the Lord.

1097
02:02:39,030 --> 02:02:40,572
May you live long!

1098
02:03:05,613 --> 02:03:07,405
Everyone get inside the gate!

1099
02:03:13,947 --> 02:03:16,488
Quick! Get inside!

1100
02:03:17,072 --> 02:03:18,530
Lord Ranganatha!

1101
02:03:31,697 --> 02:03:33,655
Move. Quickly!

1102
02:03:35,947 --> 02:03:36,947
Quickly!

1103
02:03:39,238 --> 02:03:40,697
Close the doors!

1104
02:03:40,905 --> 02:03:44,030
<i>-Everyone, get inside!</i>
 <i>-Mom! Mom!</i>

1105
02:04:09,447 --> 02:04:10,780
Govinda!

1106
02:04:11,405 --> 02:04:14,322
Lord Ranganatha!
Please protect us.

1107
02:04:16,988 --> 02:04:18,405
Govinda!

1108
02:04:19,197 --> 02:04:20,780
Sir!

1109
02:04:22,697 --> 02:04:25,697
-Mom.
-They're kids, sir. I beg you.

1110
02:04:25,988 --> 02:04:27,572
Don't do this!

1111
02:04:27,780 --> 02:04:30,572
-I beg you. Spare them, sir.
-Mom.

1112
02:04:30,905 --> 02:04:31,822
Sir!

1113
02:04:33,030 --> 02:04:36,530
-Please, sir. Let her go.
-Please leave. Please leave!

1114
02:04:46,197 --> 02:04:47,197
Please leave us.

1115
02:05:07,780 --> 02:05:10,072
Protect this Sacred Lotus.
It will protect you.

1116
02:05:10,113 --> 02:05:11,322
-Okay…
-Go, child. Go!

1117
02:05:11,405 --> 02:05:12,655
Okay, Guruji.

1118
02:05:13,363 --> 02:05:14,197
Hurry.

1119
02:05:15,363 --> 02:05:16,280
Be careful.

1120
02:05:23,905 --> 02:05:26,655
Please protect us.
Narayana!

1121
02:05:27,072 --> 02:05:28,238
Oh Lord!

1122
02:05:31,780 --> 02:05:34,405
Please protect us, Lord!

1123
02:06:58,530 --> 02:06:59,947
[in Hindi] I found it!

1124
02:08:53,405 --> 02:08:55,738
Well done, Bhairagi!

1125
02:08:56,197 --> 02:08:57,863
Well done!

1126
02:09:11,697 --> 02:09:15,697
Every word you said… has come true.

1127
02:09:26,905 --> 02:09:30,780
Now I shall rule the world
with this treasure.

1128
02:09:32,072 --> 02:09:34,988
With the corpses of these Hindus,

1129
02:09:35,488 --> 02:09:37,113
I will spread fear.

1130
02:09:37,530 --> 02:09:41,488
I will plant our flag
on this nation's soil.

1131
02:09:43,405 --> 02:09:45,947
Tell me, Bhairagi, tell me!

1132
02:09:46,238 --> 02:09:47,488
What do you desire?

1133
02:09:49,905 --> 02:09:51,613
What are you searching for, Bhairagi?

1134
02:09:58,447 --> 02:10:00,322
The Sacred Lotus.

1135
02:10:04,280 --> 02:10:05,363
What's that?

1136
02:10:08,655 --> 02:10:12,280
This treasure can only rule the earth.

1137
02:10:13,405 --> 02:10:18,155
But… the Sacred Lotus
that rested upon the Lord's navel…

1138
02:10:22,613 --> 02:10:24,947
rules the entire universe!

1139
02:10:26,155 --> 02:10:30,447
-I want that Sacred Lotus!
-You will never obtain it, Bhairagi.

1140
02:10:36,363 --> 02:10:37,488
Hey!

1141
02:10:38,613 --> 02:10:40,280
You'll never get it.

1142
02:10:41,322 --> 02:10:43,030
You'll never get it!

1143
02:10:50,488 --> 02:10:51,738
Hey, Priest…

1144
02:10:52,613 --> 02:10:54,988
tell me where the Sacred Lotus is.

1145
02:10:56,988 --> 02:11:00,238
Ranganatha, death arrives
even when uninvited.

1146
02:11:02,738 --> 02:11:05,238
Do not summon it by force.

1147
02:11:05,697 --> 02:11:07,197
You fool!

1148
02:11:08,447 --> 02:11:12,072
-You cannot decide life and death.
-Hey!

1149
02:11:12,655 --> 02:11:15,530
Only the Supreme One can.

1150
02:11:16,113 --> 02:11:17,572
Without His command

1151
02:11:18,113 --> 02:11:22,113
nothing can occur
upon this earth He created!

1152
02:11:22,488 --> 02:11:23,613
Hey, Priest!

1153
02:11:25,197 --> 02:11:26,822
Where is your God?

1154
02:11:31,072 --> 02:11:31,905
Him?

1155
02:11:34,613 --> 02:11:38,322
Does this lifeless stone
really possess such power?

1156
02:11:38,363 --> 02:11:40,488
To you, it may seem like a mere stone.

1157
02:11:41,280 --> 02:11:43,530
But it is no stone. It's not!

1158
02:11:44,822 --> 02:11:46,905
It is the source of our very breath.

1159
02:11:47,113 --> 02:11:48,988
In the wind that blows everywhere

1160
02:11:49,155 --> 02:11:51,238
in the waters that flow…

1161
02:11:52,155 --> 02:11:53,530
in every single atom…

1162
02:11:54,363 --> 02:11:56,197
the Supreme dwells everywhere.

1163
02:11:57,280 --> 02:12:00,363
Is that so? In this stone?

1164
02:12:04,780 --> 02:12:06,988
When arrogance consumes your mind,

1165
02:12:07,780 --> 02:12:09,947
death devours you.

1166
02:12:10,947 --> 02:12:12,238
Your very nature

1167
02:12:13,030 --> 02:12:15,155
turns poisonous.

1168
02:12:16,613 --> 02:12:17,863
That is when man

1169
02:12:18,863 --> 02:12:20,905
starts believing he is God.

1170
02:12:21,363 --> 02:12:22,322
God!

1171
02:12:23,572 --> 02:12:25,322
God is the Creator.

1172
02:12:26,155 --> 02:12:27,822
For upholding dharma…

1173
02:12:28,863 --> 02:12:32,113
when demons like you obstruct the path…

1174
02:12:33,572 --> 02:12:35,155
When evil crosses all limits

1175
02:12:36,113 --> 02:12:37,655
to protect righteousness

1176
02:12:39,363 --> 02:12:45,780
God incarnates Himself
to destroy vile demons like you.

1177
02:12:48,238 --> 02:12:52,613
God will descend
for your destruction as well.

1178
02:12:53,947 --> 02:12:56,530
For every head you've severed,

1179
02:12:57,863 --> 02:13:00,655
for every temple you've destroyed

1180
02:13:00,905 --> 02:13:02,988
He will settle the score.

1181
02:13:04,072 --> 02:13:06,447
He will end your reign.

1182
02:13:09,655 --> 02:13:12,072
After slaughtering everyone here,

1183
02:13:13,197 --> 02:13:14,780
and forcing us to bow down,

1184
02:13:16,197 --> 02:13:20,905
that arrogant head of yours
is swollen with pride, isn't it?

1185
02:13:21,322 --> 02:13:22,780
He will sever it

1186
02:13:23,447 --> 02:13:26,780
and cast it
into the sacred fire of Sanatana Dharma.

1187
02:13:27,030 --> 02:13:29,322
You will turn to ash. Ash!

1188
02:14:57,197 --> 02:14:58,988
Shiva!

1189
02:15:12,905 --> 02:15:14,030
It's the Sacred Lotus!

1190
02:15:23,447 --> 02:15:25,655
[Sanskrit mantras]

1191
02:15:45,322 --> 02:15:48,238
<i>♪ Timeless Bhairava</i>
 <i>Blue-throated Lord of darkness ♪</i>

1192
02:15:48,447 --> 02:15:50,988
<i>♪ Om… ♪</i>

1193
02:15:51,238 --> 02:15:54,238
<i>♪ Three-eyed one with matted locks</i>
 <i>Destroyer of time across all ages ♪</i>

1194
02:15:54,363 --> 02:15:57,238
<i>♪ Om… ♪</i>

1195
02:15:57,280 --> 02:16:00,238
<i>♪ With the thunderous beat of Damaru</i>
 <i>His roaring rhythm shakes the heavens ♪</i>

1196
02:16:00,280 --> 02:16:03,113
<i>♪ He performs the fierce Tandava</i>
 <i>May Lord Shiva bless us with peace ♪</i>

1197
02:16:03,155 --> 02:16:04,655
<i>♪ Destroyer of desire</i>
 <i>Destroyer of cities ♪</i>

1198
02:16:04,697 --> 02:16:06,197
<i>♪ Destroyer of worldly bonds</i>
 <i>Destroyer of sacrifice ♪</i>

1199
02:16:06,238 --> 02:16:07,738
<i>♪ Slayer of Gajasura</i>
 <i>Destroyer of Andhaka ♪</i>

1200
02:16:07,780 --> 02:16:09,447
<i>♪ I bow to the One</i>
 <i>Who destroys all darkness ♪</i>

1201
02:16:09,572 --> 02:16:10,738
<i>♪ Hara Hara Hara Hara Hara! ♪</i>

1202
02:16:10,780 --> 02:16:13,155
<i>♪ The storm clouds of war</i>
 <i>Tear through the skies ♪</i>

1203
02:16:15,530 --> 02:16:18,822
<i>♪ Hara Hara Hara Hara Hara!</i>
 <i>The gates of hell swing wide ♪</i>

1204
02:16:21,530 --> 02:16:24,447
<i>♪ Hara Hara Hara Hara!</i>
 <i>A weapon forged for the great battle ♪</i>

1205
02:16:24,572 --> 02:16:27,322
<i>♪ Gham Gham Gham Gham Gham!</i>
 <i>The force that crushes every calamity ♪</i>

1206
02:16:27,530 --> 02:16:28,780
<i>♪ Gana Gana Gana Gana Gana! ♪</i>

1207
02:16:28,822 --> 02:16:32,155
<i>♪ Bearers of the sacred Lingam</i>
 <i>Devotees of Gangadhara ♪</i>

1208
02:16:32,780 --> 02:16:35,572
<i>♪ The Himalayas are His abode ♪</i>

1209
02:16:35,780 --> 02:16:38,530
<i>♪ Eternity echoes in His name ♪</i>

1210
02:16:38,697 --> 02:16:41,572
<i>♪ We worship, we surrender ♪</i>

1211
02:16:41,822 --> 02:16:43,530
<i>♪ Harom Hara! ♪</i>

1212
02:16:44,697 --> 02:16:50,572
<i>♪ The body itself is Shiva’s temple</i>
 <i>Every atom is filled with Shiva ♪</i>

1213
02:16:50,780 --> 02:16:54,947
<i>♪ The Trident stands forever</i>
 <i>As our shield and guiding force ♪</i>

1214
02:16:59,947 --> 02:17:02,863
<i>♪ Veera Naga</i>
 <i>The secret army of Rudra ♪</i>

1215
02:17:02,905 --> 02:17:05,822
<i>♪ Vaira Naga</i>
 <i>The doom that unleashes hell ♪</i>

1216
02:17:05,863 --> 02:17:08,947
<i>♪ Swaira Naga</i>
 <i>The destiny of a thousand births ♪</i>

1217
02:17:09,030 --> 02:17:11,780
<i>♪ Fierce Naga! Divine Naga! ♪</i>

1218
02:17:11,863 --> 02:17:14,863
<i>♪ Veera Naga</i>
 <i>The secret army of Rudra ♪</i>

1219
02:17:14,988 --> 02:17:17,822
<i>♪ Vaira Naga</i>
 <i>The doom that unleashes hell ♪</i>

1220
02:17:17,863 --> 02:17:20,905
<i>♪ Swaira Naga</i>
 <i>The destiny of a thousand births ♪</i>

1221
02:17:20,988 --> 02:17:23,530
<i>♪ Steadfast Naga! Supreme Naga! ♪</i>

1222
02:17:23,572 --> 02:17:27,155
<i>♪ Om! Salutations to Rudra</i>
 <i>Salutations to the Mighty One ♪</i>

1223
02:17:27,280 --> 02:17:30,238
<i>♪ Salutations to Bhairava</i>
 <i>Salutations to the Fierce One ♪</i>

1224
02:17:30,322 --> 02:17:33,238
<i>♪ Salutations to the Slayer of Time</i>
 <i>Salutations to the Clad-in-Hide One ♪</i>

1225
02:17:33,405 --> 02:17:36,238
<i>♪ Salutations to the Lord of Beings</i>
 <i>Salutations to the Embodiment of Time ♪</i>

1226
02:17:36,405 --> 02:17:38,905
<i>♪ Salutations to the Lord of Spirits</i>
 <i>Salutations to the Master of All Life ♪</i>

1227
02:17:38,947 --> 02:17:42,155
<i>♪ Salutations to the Destroyer of Time</i>
 <i>Salutations to the Blue-Throated One ♪</i>

1228
02:17:42,238 --> 02:17:44,947
<i>♪ Salutations to the Fearsome One</i>
 <i>Salutations to the Benign One ♪</i>

1229
02:17:45,030 --> 02:17:49,738
<i>♪ Our endless reverence</i>
 <i>To the Sky-Clad Lord ♪</i>

1230
02:17:50,072 --> 02:17:51,738
Sacred…

1231
02:17:52,988 --> 02:17:54,780
Lotus…

1232
02:17:59,863 --> 02:18:00,822
Stop!

1233
02:18:07,280 --> 02:18:09,613
Our dharma is eternal.

1234
02:18:10,238 --> 02:18:12,780
Our deity is eternal.

1235
02:18:13,530 --> 02:18:16,363
Our lives are an offering to Lord Shiva.

1236
02:18:17,363 --> 02:18:19,947
Our courage lies
in protecting Hindu dharma.

1237
02:18:22,530 --> 02:18:26,155
Lord Shankara of Kailasa himself
descended as Kaladi Shankara…

1238
02:18:26,697 --> 02:18:30,280
The shield of protection
he bestowed upon this Vedic land…

1239
02:18:30,822 --> 02:18:32,988
is the Naga Sadhu way of life.

1240
02:18:35,905 --> 02:18:39,780
We have attained the supreme state
by inhaling within our breath,

1241
02:18:40,113 --> 02:18:44,530
the primal Rudra energies
that govern the cosmos itself.

1242
02:18:46,405 --> 02:18:48,822
This land is the abode of saffron.

1243
02:18:49,322 --> 02:18:50,822
A sanctuary of dharma.

1244
02:18:51,655 --> 02:18:55,072
Whenever Hindu society loses its way
and devotion weakens,

1245
02:18:55,530 --> 02:18:59,530
ours is the lineage of Adi Shankaracharya,

1246
02:19:00,322 --> 02:19:03,488
born from the union
of spiritual power and penance.

1247
02:19:07,322 --> 02:19:10,572
Hindutva is not a religion.
It is benevolence.

1248
02:19:11,322 --> 02:19:16,072
The destruction of the heretical forces
that seek to harm it…

1249
02:19:16,655 --> 02:19:18,113
is our sole purpose!

1250
02:19:28,405 --> 02:19:32,238
Endless madness is raging with arrogance.

1251
02:19:32,988 --> 02:19:36,738
It marched to spill blood
across this saffron land.

1252
02:19:39,030 --> 02:19:43,113
With the command of Adi Shankaracharya
and the blessings of Adiyogi,

1253
02:19:43,780 --> 02:19:46,155
let’s rip open the hearts
of those desert men!

1254
02:19:46,822 --> 02:19:49,780
If they so much as dream
of setting foot in these Himalayas,

1255
02:19:50,322 --> 02:19:52,738
we'll show them
not even their bones will be found!

1256
02:19:56,072 --> 02:19:57,655
Let's show them what happens

1257
02:19:57,697 --> 02:19:59,155
when this Vedic land
becomes a battlefield!

1258
02:20:01,113 --> 02:20:02,738
Let's prove that

1259
02:20:03,280 --> 02:20:05,738
heads are bound to roll
when Shiva's army marches!

1260
02:20:08,447 --> 02:20:11,738
Let us unleash the valor
of Sanatana Dharma in our blood

1261
02:20:12,197 --> 02:20:15,072
and dye the Himalayan snow
red with theirs!

1262
02:20:16,822 --> 02:20:19,780
For the protection of dharma,
let us all become Rudras of Time!

1263
02:20:21,113 --> 02:20:23,655
[in Sanskrit] This is the Eternal Dharma!

1264
02:20:23,905 --> 02:20:26,488
This is the Eternal Dharma!

1265
02:20:26,947 --> 02:20:29,655
Hara Hara Mahadev!

1266
02:20:29,697 --> 02:20:33,530
[all] Hara Hara Mahadev!

1267
02:20:33,572 --> 02:20:36,155
[all] Hara Hara Mahadev!

1268
02:20:38,613 --> 02:20:41,155
Is this the Sacred Lotus, Bhairagi?

1269
02:20:42,613 --> 02:20:44,738
Yes, this is it.
Yes, this is the one.

1270
02:20:45,488 --> 02:20:46,363
Wow!

1271
02:20:46,697 --> 02:20:49,072
Does this Sacred Lotus

1272
02:20:49,113 --> 02:20:52,447
truly possess the power
to rule the universe, Bhairagi?

1273
02:20:53,780 --> 02:20:54,697
Yes!

1274
02:20:55,613 --> 02:20:57,363
I can't believe it.

1275
02:20:58,363 --> 02:21:01,363
The universe doesn't run
on your belief, Abdali.

1276
02:21:03,363 --> 02:21:07,155
This Sacred Lotus is the key
to the great divine gateway,

1277
02:21:07,863 --> 02:21:09,613
created by Brahma.

1278
02:21:10,030 --> 02:21:13,322
By invoking Adisesha's serpent lineages,

1279
02:21:13,447 --> 02:21:18,030
the eight-direction mantra Serpent seal

1280
02:21:18,155 --> 02:21:19,572
is now released.

1281
02:21:35,238 --> 02:21:36,905
The Serpent seal?

1282
02:21:40,947 --> 02:21:42,280
[in Hindi] What is that?

1283
02:21:44,363 --> 02:21:47,655
To the north of the Himalayan peaks,

1284
02:21:48,113 --> 02:21:50,863
at the foothills of Mount Kailash,

1285
02:21:51,030 --> 02:21:53,738
there's the hidden temple
of that Virata Purusha.

1286
02:21:54,363 --> 02:21:55,405
Right there…

1287
02:21:55,822 --> 02:21:59,155
is the divine gateway
which was sealed by the Serpent seal.

1288
02:22:00,405 --> 02:22:03,030
After the Dwapara Yuga ended,

1289
02:22:03,238 --> 02:22:06,280
to prevent humans
from entering that gateway,

1290
02:22:06,447 --> 02:22:09,905
while the enlightened sages
performed a grand ritual

1291
02:22:10,197 --> 02:22:12,863
using their mystical powers
during the 200th full moon,

1292
02:22:12,905 --> 02:22:16,613
the Sacred Lotus
emerged from the sacred fire.

1293
02:22:23,613 --> 02:22:26,947
They sealed
the divine gateway with that ritual.

1294
02:22:27,405 --> 02:22:29,363
Fearing that evil forces in the Kali Yuga

1295
02:22:29,488 --> 02:22:32,697
might seize the Sacred Lotus
and open the gateway,

1296
02:22:32,905 --> 02:22:36,780
they invoked the most powerful serpents

1297
02:22:37,363 --> 02:22:39,113
and sealed it using the Serpent seal.

1298
02:22:39,780 --> 02:22:42,863
They inscribed the Garuda mantras,
used to unseal the Serpent seal,

1299
02:22:43,030 --> 02:22:46,155
in tantric script
upon palm-leaf manuscripts,

1300
02:22:46,405 --> 02:22:48,113
and placed the Sacred Lotus…

1301
02:22:48,863 --> 02:22:51,530
Install this Sacred Lotus

1302
02:22:52,072 --> 02:22:54,613
in the Sri Ranganatha Swamy temple.

1303
02:22:57,863 --> 02:23:00,822
They installed it in the foremost
among the 108 Vaishnava temples,

1304
02:23:00,988 --> 02:23:04,655
the Ranganatha Temple of Srirangapuram…

1305
02:23:07,322 --> 02:23:10,030
To unseal the Serpent seal,

1306
02:23:10,155 --> 02:23:13,947
we must install the Sacred Lotus
upon the golden pedestal,

1307
02:23:14,072 --> 02:23:18,655
and chant the Garuda mantras
before the 200th full moon.

1308
02:23:18,780 --> 02:23:21,655
Only then can
the divine gateway be opened.

1309
02:23:21,905 --> 02:23:23,363
Otherwise…

1310
02:23:29,697 --> 02:23:33,613
Anyway… what lies
beyond that gateway, Bhairagi?

1311
02:23:44,363 --> 02:23:45,572
[in Hindi] There are many here!

1312
02:24:35,613 --> 02:24:39,738
[Sanskrit mantra chanting]

1313
02:25:08,613 --> 02:25:10,572
What is happening, Bhairagi?

1314
02:25:10,863 --> 02:25:13,030
Prepare the army at once, Abdali.

1315
02:25:13,322 --> 02:25:16,572
We must leave this place immediately.
Take the Sacred Lotus.

1316
02:25:51,530 --> 02:25:52,738
<i>♪ Hara! ♪</i>

1317
02:25:53,405 --> 02:25:55,155
<i>♪ Hara! Hara! ♪</i>

1318
02:25:56,530 --> 02:25:57,905
<i>♪ Hara! Hara! ♪</i>

1319
02:26:07,447 --> 02:26:09,488
The Naga Sadhus…

1320
02:28:04,280 --> 02:28:06,655
<i>♪ Veera Naga</i>
 <i>The secret army of Rudra ♪</i>

1321
02:28:06,697 --> 02:28:09,113
<i>♪ Vaira Naga</i>
 <i>The doom that unleashes hell ♪</i>

1322
02:28:09,155 --> 02:28:11,655
<i>♪ Swaira Naga</i>
 <i>The destiny of a thousand births ♪</i>

1323
02:28:11,697 --> 02:28:14,113
<i>♪ Fierce Naga! Divine Naga! ♪</i>

1324
02:28:14,155 --> 02:28:16,780
<i>♪ Veera Naga</i>
 <i>The secret army of Rudra ♪</i>

1325
02:28:16,822 --> 02:28:18,988
<i>♪ Vaira Naga</i>
 <i>The doom that unleashes hell ♪</i>

1326
02:28:19,155 --> 02:28:21,947
Hara Hara Mahadev!

1327
02:29:31,322 --> 02:29:33,488
Shiva!

1328
02:29:53,697 --> 02:29:55,530
Shiva!

1329
02:30:05,655 --> 02:30:07,488
Shiva!

1330
02:31:02,280 --> 02:31:03,572
Bhairagi!

1331
02:31:04,322 --> 02:31:09,530
Until you undo this serpent's seal,
no one can stop you.

1332
02:31:11,280 --> 02:31:12,238
Go!

1333
02:32:23,613 --> 02:32:24,572
Hey!

1334
02:32:24,655 --> 02:32:27,655
If you are the guardian
of this Serpent seal,

1335
02:32:27,780 --> 02:32:30,947
then I am the demon
who rules this earth!

1336
02:32:31,947 --> 02:32:37,197
I heard no one could get past
the Naga Sadhus and enter inside.

1337
02:32:38,822 --> 02:32:40,322
Well, he did.

1338
02:32:56,863 --> 02:33:02,197
[Sanskrit shloka]

1339
02:33:15,072 --> 02:33:19,030
[Sanskrit chanting continues]

1340
02:33:22,447 --> 02:33:26,030
You roam around
with ash smeared on your body.

1341
02:33:26,322 --> 02:33:27,488
You're worthless.

1342
02:33:28,447 --> 02:33:31,738
And what is your invisible God worth?

1343
02:33:37,780 --> 02:33:40,405
Are you mighty enough
to rule the five elements?

1344
02:33:41,655 --> 02:33:44,530
Though you destroyed our temples,

1345
02:33:45,280 --> 02:33:47,280
you cannot destroy our dharma.

1346
02:33:48,363 --> 02:33:50,488
We worship the Sun.

1347
02:33:52,072 --> 02:33:53,488
Can you stop it?

1348
02:33:56,155 --> 02:33:58,030
We worship the Earth.

1349
02:33:58,655 --> 02:34:00,072
Can you uproot it?

1350
02:34:03,405 --> 02:34:05,697
We worship the rivers.

1351
02:34:06,905 --> 02:34:08,447
Can you drain them?

1352
02:34:11,030 --> 02:34:13,155
We worship the forests.

1353
02:34:13,405 --> 02:34:15,238
Can you cut them all down?

1354
02:34:17,155 --> 02:34:19,488
The air we breathe is God.

1355
02:34:19,697 --> 02:34:21,905
The fire that burns is God.

1356
02:34:22,155 --> 02:34:25,697
God is the source
of this universe's salvation

1357
02:34:26,030 --> 02:34:28,113
and its annihilation.

1358
02:34:28,738 --> 02:34:29,738
Ultimately,

1359
02:34:30,363 --> 02:34:35,280
If you take our lives, the God who
gave us life will end His own.

1360
02:34:35,363 --> 02:34:36,780
Then call him here!

1361
02:36:22,572 --> 02:36:27,238
[in Sanskrit] Before the sacred idol
of Mahagaruda, all venom is subdued.

1362
02:37:33,822 --> 02:37:36,197
Destroyer and remover of poison,
let it be destroyed.

1363
02:37:37,405 --> 02:37:40,030
The poison has perished.
All of it has vanished.

1364
02:37:40,572 --> 02:37:43,488
The poison is destroyed,
the venom is slain.

1365
02:37:44,030 --> 02:37:46,363
By the sacred invocation,
the poison is vanquished.

1366
02:37:46,947 --> 02:37:49,697
May it be struck down
by Indra’s thunderbolt!

1367
02:38:07,488 --> 02:38:11,197
[in Sanskrit] Before the sacred idol
of Mahagaruda, all poison is subdued.

1368
02:38:47,405 --> 02:38:50,863
<i>Hara Hara Mahadev!</i>

1369
02:39:04,197 --> 02:39:06,113
[in Sanskrit] Move forth, move forth.

1370
02:39:06,197 --> 02:39:10,113
Doer of all deeds,
embodiment of every poison…

1371
02:39:11,280 --> 02:39:13,238
Corrupter of poison, nourisher of poison.

1372
02:39:30,113 --> 02:39:32,530
[in Sanskrit] Sever the serpent bonds.

1373
02:39:33,072 --> 02:39:35,113
Release us from the serpent’s snare.

1374
02:39:35,447 --> 02:39:37,572
Sever the serpent--

1375
02:40:34,405 --> 02:40:36,988
Bhairagi!

1376
02:41:15,988 --> 02:41:17,322
Riya!

1377
02:41:21,530 --> 02:41:23,197
Riya! Riya!

1378
02:41:26,981 --> 02:41:29,315
[Sanskrit chanting]

1379
02:41:41,197 --> 02:41:43,822
Revered in all three worlds.

1380
02:41:44,030 --> 02:41:47,238
The fierce and dreadful One,
blazing like the fire of doom.

1381
02:41:47,405 --> 02:41:48,988
To the Lord of adamantine claws!

1382
02:41:49,238 --> 02:41:50,988
The One with the mighty beak!

1383
02:42:00,655 --> 02:42:01,947
Riya! Are you okay?

1384
02:42:03,738 --> 02:42:04,655
Riya!

1385
02:42:04,947 --> 02:42:06,780
[in Sanskrit] Sever the serpent bonds.

1386
02:42:06,988 --> 02:42:09,488
Release us from the serpent’s snare.

1387
02:44:02,113 --> 02:44:04,363
Abdali! Abdali…

1388
02:44:28,988 --> 02:44:31,447
<i>God is watching everything.</i>

1389
02:44:31,655 --> 02:44:35,447
<i>He will definitely punish you.</i>

1390
02:44:58,322 --> 02:45:00,988
You can't even look directly at the sun.

1391
02:45:01,322 --> 02:45:03,988
How dare you speak ill of the God
whose vision is as wide spread?

1392
02:45:04,572 --> 02:45:06,738
You can't even touch fire.

1393
02:45:07,030 --> 02:45:09,697
How dare you seek to destroy
the God whose eyes are fire?

1394
02:45:10,155 --> 02:45:13,155
You are but a scavenging dog
searching for scraps in the desert.

1395
02:45:13,488 --> 02:45:16,863
And you dare challenge the Lord
who sustains the infinite universe?

1396
02:45:17,363 --> 02:45:20,155
Hey! We are Hindus.

1397
02:45:20,363 --> 02:45:23,822
Righteousness is our way of life.
Compassion is our nature.

1398
02:45:24,113 --> 02:45:26,655
We shelter anyone who seeks refuge.

1399
02:45:26,822 --> 02:45:29,322
We help anyone who asks for aid.

1400
02:45:29,572 --> 02:45:33,155
But if you mistake that kindness
for weakness and raise your sword…

1401
02:45:33,280 --> 02:45:37,113
we will turn your heads into skulls
and wear them around our necks.

1402
02:45:37,322 --> 02:45:39,322
This alone is eternal!

1403
02:45:39,405 --> 02:45:42,447
<i>Hara Hara Mahadev!</i>

1404
02:45:42,780 --> 02:45:46,072
<i>Hara Hara Mahadev!</i>

1405
02:45:57,988 --> 02:46:00,905
So… what lies behind that door, Aunt?

1406
02:46:01,197 --> 02:46:04,822
To know that, we must know what transpired

1407
02:46:05,113 --> 02:46:09,113
between the end of the Dwapara Yuga
and the dawn of the Kali Yuga.